hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5011","(5011) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhiyal, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He killed her while he was praying, he said: And he said His commander: If she does not present herself to you, do not kill her."
"5012","(5012) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: Kill her while you are praying."
"5013","(5013) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said about the scorpion. The man saw it while praying. He said: Turn it away from you. I said: So if it refuses? He said: Leave her away. I said: What if she refuses? He said: Then kill her, and wash the place where you killed her."
"5014","(5014) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of his leaders; That Muwarriq killed her while he was praying."
"5015","(5015) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about killing a scorpion during prayer? He said: There is busyness in prayer."
"5016","(5016) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tamim bin Mahmoud, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Shibl, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade a man to live in a place and pray in it as he lives in it. The camel"
"5017","(5017) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He did not use a place to pray in his house."
"5018","(5018) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Nabih, on the authority of Jumman, who said: I saw Sa’d come many times while the people were Prayer, so he walked between the row and the wall until he came to his place of prayer, and he was praying at the fifth cylinder."
"5019","(5019) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazid, who said: I saw Al-Miswar bin Makhramah After the prayer is performed, he moves through the rows until he reaches the second or first."
"5020","(5020) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salih Al-Tamar, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad adhering to one person praying. He prays in the mosque and does not pray in any other place, and I saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab doing that."
"5021","(5021) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a people whose ship was shipwrecked, so they continued to pray while they were in the water? He said: They nod, but if they go out naked? He said: They pray sitting."
"5022","(5022) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Mujahid; That Omar bin Abdul Aziz asked him about a people whose ship was shipwrecked, so they went out, and the time for prayer came? He said: Their imam will be the easiest of them, and they will line up in one line, and each man of them will cover himself with his left hand. His private parts without touching the private parts."
"5023","(5023) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the people, the ship will crash among them, so they will go out naked. How will they pray? He said: Sitting, with their imam in the middle, and they prostrate and lower their eyes."
"5024","(5024) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Yazid, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning the naked ones, he said: They pray sitting, gesticulating, and their imam stands in the middle of them."
"5025","(5025) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hamran, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A drowning person prostrates on a surface of water."
"5026","(5026) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Bathing on Friday is obligatory for every mature person. (Bukhari 2465. Ibn Majah 1089)"
"5027","(5027) Hushaym told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Ziyad informed us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Single, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is a right upon Muslims; That one of them should bathe on the day of Friday, and that he should touch some perfume if his family has it, and if he does not have it. It is good, so water is good. (Tirmidhi 528. Ahmad 4/282)"
"5028","(5028) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Hassan bin Atiyya told us, he said: Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, He said: Aws bin Aws Al-Thaqafi told me, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever washes on Friday He bathed, rose early and rose early, and walked but did not ride, so he approached the imam and listened and did not neglect. He had every step of the Sunnah. The reward for her fasting and standing. (Tirmidhi 4961 Abu Dawud 349)"
"5029","(5029) Sharik and Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Wathhab, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever comes to the congregational prayer, let him wash himself. (Nasa’i 1680)"
"5030","(5030) Ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; In the same way (Bukhari 8771, Muslim 579)"
"5031","(5031) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: It is the right of every Muslim to perform ablution every seven days, and that is the day of Friday prayer. (Nasa’i 1669. Ahmad 3/304)"
"5032","(5032) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Shaybah, on the authority of Talq, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Washing is done four times; From impurity, cupping, washing the dead, and washing the congregation."
"5033","(5033) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Khalil advised me. By washing on Friday. (Abu Ali 6198)"
"5034","(5034) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; Omar bin Al-Khattab was giving a Friday sermon when a man came and Omar said: Why are you abstaining from praying? The man said: It is only that I heard the call and performed ablution. He said: And ablution as well. Did you not listen to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to say: If one of you goes to the congregation, let him perform ablution. (Bukhari 882 and Muslim 580)"
"5035","(5035) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: I heard Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Thawban, He narrated on the authority of a man from the Ansar, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: There are three rights upon every Muslim: Washing on Friday, using the siwak, and applying perfume if any. (Bukhari 880. Ahmad 4/34)"
"5036","(5036) Hushaym told us, he said: Yazid bin Abi Ziyad told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: I was with Ibn Saad, his son came to him and said to him: Did you wash? He said: No, I performed ablution, then came, and Saad said to him: I did not think that anyone would neglect washing on Friday."
"5037","(5037) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: A man from among the immigrants came on the day of Friday. Then Omar said to him: Did you wash? He said: No. He said: You knew that we were commanded otherwise. The man said: What were you commanded to do? He said: By washing. He said: Are you a group of immigrants, or people? He said: I don't know. (Abdul Razzaq 5293)"
"5038","(5038) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: While Omar bin The speaker delivers a sermon, then he mentions something similar to it."
"5039","(5039) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Ammar spoke to a man, but he continued. Ali, and he said: So, you are one of those who do not wash on Friday."
"5040","(5040) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Zazan, he said: Ali was asked about washing on the day of Friday? He said: Washing on the day of Friday, on the two Eids, and on the day of Arafah."
"5041","(5041) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu Al-Walid Abdullah bin Al-Harith; He heard Ibn Abbas say: I did not feel that anyone thought that he had any purity on the day of Friday other than washing."
"5042","(5042) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Ziyad al-Numayri, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: They will bathe on the day of Friday. Even if a cup is worth a dinar."
"5043","(5043) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Ka’b said: He panics for the day of Friday. Everything except heavy things, and every person who dreams about it must perform ghusl."
"5044","(5044) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amrah bint Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was People serve themselves, and one of them was going with his body to the gathering, and it was said to them: If only you had washed yourself. (Bukhari 9031 Muslim 6)"
"5045","(5045) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: It is obligatory for every Muslim to wash himself. One day among seven days, and it is Friday."
"5046","(5046) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Omar said about something: You are worse than one who does not wash. Friday"
"5047","(5047) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to prefer performing ablution on the day of Friday."
"5048","(5048) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Nu’man ibn Sa’d, on the authority of his brother Abdullah ibn Sa’d. He said: Whenever Omar swore, he would say: I am worse than one who does not wash on the day of Friday."
"5049","(5049) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Misra, he said: I asked) about washing the day of Friday, is it a Sunnah? He said: The Muslims were washing, so I repeated it, but he did not add anything to me when he said: The Muslims were washing. So I knew that it was something that Muslims liked, and not according to Sunnah."
"5050","(5050) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, who said: Washing The day of Friday, the day of Al-Adha, the day of Fitr, the day of Arafah, and the day of entering Mecca."
"5051","(5051) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: They used to love when they saw the hardships Not to neglect washing on Friday."
"5052","(5052) Hushaym told us, he said: Ubad Allah ibn Umar informed us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever goes to the congregation, let him take a bath. (Ahmad 2/551 Tabarani 13392)"
"5053","(5053) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mughra’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He used to take a bath while he was in the iron on Friday."
"5054","(5054) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: Ibn Sibaq informed me; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said in a gathering of people: This is a day of Eid, so take a bath, and whoever is with him. It is good, so it does not harm him if he touches it, and you should use the siwak."
"5055","(5055) Muhammad bin Bishr and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal said: She should be washed and perfumed, if necessary."
"5056","(5056) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Zaid, he said: I said to Abdul Rahman: Is there any ritual ablution other than the day of Friday? He said: Yes, the Day of Sacrifice, the Day of Fitr, and the Day of Arafah."
"5057","(5057) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father; He used to recommend washing on the Eid and Friday prayers."
"5058","(5058) Muhammad bin Bishr and Ibn Fudail narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Hammam bin Al-Harith, he said: Abdullah said: It is part of the Sunnah to wash on the day of Friday prayer. (Abdul Razzaq 5316. Tayalisi 391)"
"5059","(5059) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a Friday sermon, and said: Whoever goes to the Friday prayer, let him wash himself."
"5060","(5060) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ali bin Rifa’i, on the authority of Hayyan Al-Araj, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: Perhaps I found it cold on Friday, so I did not wash myself. (Nasa’i 1405)"
"5061","(5061) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi (h), and Ubaydah and Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Abd al-Malik, on the authority of a gift; They said: Whoever performs ablution on the day of Friday is good, and whoever performs ablution, then ablution is better."
"5062","(5062) Hushaym told us, he said: Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Abu Wael, he said: They mentioned washing the day of Friday. With him, Abu Wael said: It is not obligatory, perhaps an old man will have to bathe in the extreme cold on Friday. When he died"
"5063","(5063) Hushaym told us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He did not consider washing obligatory, except for ritual impurity."
"5064","(5064) Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Samurah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs ablution on the day of Friday, it will be blessed and blessed, and whoever washes himself, that is better. (Abu Dawud 358. Ahmad 5/16)"
"5065","(5065) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever performs ablution and performs it well, then comes to the congregation and comes close and listens and listens, his sins between him and them will be forgiven. The last Friday, and an additional three days, and whoever touches pebbles has negated it. (Muslim 27 Abu Dawud 1043)"
"5066","(5066) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I asked him about the Friday prayer? He said: Bathing is not obligatory except in the case of ritual impurity."
"5067","(5067) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Atiya, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: Whoever purifies himself and purifies himself well, then comes to the congregation and does not distract himself or ignore it, he will be an expiator for what between it and the other congregation, and the five prayers are expiations for what is between them, and in the congregation there is an hour that does not agree with it. A Muslim servant asks God for something good, but He gives it to him. (Abdullah bin Hamid 901)"
"5068","(5068) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He did not wash himself on Friday while traveling."
"5069","(5069) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar (h) and on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn age; He did not wash himself on Friday while traveling."
"5070","(5070) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of his maternal uncle Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Jubayr bin Mutim ; He did not wash himself on Friday while traveling."
"5071","(5071) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith; Mujahid and Tawus did not wash themselves while traveling on Friday, but Sa`id bin Jubayr used to wash himself when traveling. He was brought captive."
"5072","(5072) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Al-Qasim about washing on the day of Friday prayer while traveling? He said: Ibn Omar did not wash, and I think to you that you should not wash."
"5073","(5073) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad; Al-Aswad and Al-Alqamah did not wash themselves on Friday while traveling."
"5074","(5074) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah, he said: The ritual ablution is only for Who attended the gathering?"
"5075","(5075) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Jasra, who said: I asked Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith about Bathing on Friday? He said: Abdullah bin Al-Harith used to wash himself on Fridays when he was traveling or at home."
"5076","(5076) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ma’dan, who said: I heard a beloved and a man asked him: What do you say about washing? Friday prayer, is it obligatory? He said: I saw Talq coming from Mecca to Al-Hajjaj as a captive, and he did not neglect to wash on the day of Friday."
"5077","(5077) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; He used to wash himself every Friday while traveling."
"5078","(5078) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Yahya, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ziyad bin Hudayr, who said: I covered He was on a journey on Friday, so he took a bath."
"5079","(5079) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he performs ablution on Friday after dawn comes from Impurity, its sufficiency is that of ghusl on the day of Friday."
"5080","(5080) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Abd al-Malik, About giving; They said: If a man performs ablution on Friday after dawn has come, that is sufficient for the Friday ablution."
"5081","(5081) Hushaym told us, saying: Habib bin Abi Al-Aali told us, on the authority of Mujahid; Like that"
"5082","(5082) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: If he performs ablution after dawn, that is sufficient for the ritual ablution of the day. Friday"
"5083","(5083) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: Whoever takes a bath on Friday after dawn has come Part of the Friday ghusl."
"5084","(5084) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Bashir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He was asked about a man who took a bath on Friday with magic? He said: It is sufficient."
"5085","(5085) Hushaym told us, he said: The common people told us, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymiy, he said: They used to love the one who took a bath. On the day of the Friday prayer, that there should not be any dispute between him and the Friday prayer. He said: And they used to say: If he breaks the prayer after washing, He returned to the state he was in before he took a bath."
"5086","(5086) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; Concerning a man who takes a bath on Friday, then he performs the ritual bath. He said: He repeats the bath."
"5087","(5087) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdah bin Abi Lubab, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza. On the authority of his father; He used to wash himself on Fridays, then he would freshen his hair after washing, and then he would not repeat the washing."
"5088","(5088) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Muhammad did not like it to be between him and Friday is an event. Al-Hasan said: If he breaks his fast, he performs ablution."
"5089","(5089) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he performs ablution on a Friday, then he does its parts. Ablution"
"5090","(5090) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Nabil, she said: I heard Ibn Umar and his two sons Saad bin Abi Waqqas, They say to the women: Whoever of you comes in congregation, let her bathe."
"5091","(5091) Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to order his wives to wash themselves on Fridays."
"5092","(5092) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; In the same way"
"5093","(5093) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Women do not have to wash on Fridays."
"5094","(5094) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Zufar bin Muhajir Al-Ghadiri, who said: He was the brother of the chief of his family, both men and women. By washing on Friday."
"5095","(5095) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to bathe once for ritual impurity and for Friday prayers."
"5096","(5096) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Mawali, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Muslim, who said: The sons of My brother Urwah ibn al-Zubayr used to wash in the bathroom on Friday, and Urwah said: O my brother’s sons, it was only You washed yourself in the bathroom to remove dirt, so wash for the congregation."
"5097","(5097) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada told me, he said: My mother told me, That her father told her that one of the sons of my father Qatadah entered upon him on Friday to wash his head, and he said: For Friday, did you wash? He said: No, but on his own behalf. He said: So prepare a bath for the congregation."
"5098","(5098) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: He said: Ali: There is no jum’ah, no tashreeq except in a comprehensive Egypt."
"5099","(5099) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: No plural, no Tashreeq, nor the breaking of the fast prayer, nor the sacrifice of sacrifice, except in a mosque in Egypt, or a great city.\nHajjaj said: I heard Ataa say something like that."
"5100","(5100) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Not Ali. The people of the villages are plural, but the plural is for the people of cities, such as cities."
"5101","(5101) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They both said: Friday prayers in the cities."
"5102","(5102) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked: What about all the idiots? He said: No."
"5103","(5103) Hushaym told us, saying: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad; He sent a message to the people of Dhul-Halif: not to gather with it, but to enter the mosque, the mosque of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace."
"5104","(5104) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not gather in the armies."
"5105","(5105) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no plural, nor sunrise, except in Egypt. A mosque"
"5106","(5106) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidy, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman Al-Salami, on the authority of Ali, He said: There is no sharīq, nor plural except in a comprehensive Egypt."
"5107","(5107) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Al-Ray is from Egypt."
"5108","(5108) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Maimounah, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; They wrote to Omar asking him about the congregation? So he wrote: Gather together wherever you are."
"5109","(5109) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to Adiy bin Adiy, either The people of the village are not the people of Amud. They should move, so appoint a commander over them to gather them together."
"5110","(5110) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Maqil, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a town is attached to one another, they will gather together."
"5111","(5111) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Malik, who said: The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, were in this water. They unite between Mecca and Medina."
"5112","(5112) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I sent to Aisha bin Saad, to ask her about Friday? She said: Saad was at the head of seven or eight miles, and sometimes he would come to it, and sometimes he would not. He comes to her."
"5113","(5113) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Amir Al-Muzani told us, he said: I heard Nafi’, narrating on the authority of Ibn Omar; He said: The Friday prayer is upon the one who has been given comfort."
"5114","(5114) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Masruq, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Friday prayer is given from two farsakhin."
"5115","(5115) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yazeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I asked him: On whom? Is Friday prayer obligatory? He said: On the one who heard the call."
"5116","(5116) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: I saw a man watching the congregation from the corner, and two farsangs of Insight"
"5117","(5117) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Abu Al-Malih used to work on the idiots, so when the congregation came, he would gather From us"
"5118","(5118) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Muslim al-Abdi, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: The Friday prayer is given from four farsakhs."
"5119","(5119) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: We used to come to her from Two parsecs."
"5120","(5120) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Friday prayer applies to everyone who has taken refuge in the night. His family"
"5121","(5121) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umayr, on the authority of Umar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The Friday prayer is for the one who took refuge in the night to his family."
"5122","(5122) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: My father used to be in Urwa’s well for three days. Miles from Medina, neither a group nor a group of people witnessed it."
"5123","(5123) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Qur’a ibn Khalid, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah Mawla Abu Ayyub said: Ibn Salam used to come to us on Friday, and he would hang with him a container of water and collect some water. Al-Awaliya."
"5124","(5124) Rawad bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The gang was made up of men. The women gather with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and they do not arrive on their journey until the next day. (Abu Dawud 52)"
"5125","(5125) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: The Friday prayer is for the one who takes shelter at night to his family."
"5126","(5126) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of his father; Abdullah bin Rawahi used to come to the gathering walking, so I said to Abdul Hamid: How long was he between his two houses? And between the group? He said: Two miles."
"5127","(5127) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; They used to bear witness in congregation with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Dhul-Halif. (Abdul Razzaq 5151)"
"5128","(5128) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hawshab bin Aqeel al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: I asked Ata’: How much do you give the Friday prayer? He said: From seven miles."
"5129","(5129) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I said to Al-Zuhri: On whom is the congregation obligatory upon those who are near? The city? He said: The people of Dhul-Halifah used to give the Friday prayers."
"5130","(5130) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad was asked about the man, and he collected from this The chutes? He says: The Ansar used to gather from the graveyards around Medina."
"5131","(5131) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Hammad about a man who collects two farshins? He said: No. And I asked the referee? He said: If he comes and goes on a single day, then he must join it."
"5132","(5132) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayoub bin Utbah, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Huraira, he said: The Friday prayer is given from two farsakhin."
"5133","(5133) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: Not Ali. Whoever is at the top of a mile is gathered."
"5134","(5134) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; He was witnessing the gathering in Taif while he was in a village called Al-Wahat, at the top of three miles."
"5135","(5135) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qays Al-Fara’i, who said: I heard Amr bin Shuaib, it was said to him: O father Ibrahim, on whom is it obligatory to join prayers? He said: On the one who heard the voice."
"5136","(5136) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: The traveler is not obligated to join the prayer."
"5137","(5137) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not combine prayers while traveling."
"5138","(5138) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of an alcoholic person, who said: The traveler is not required to sacrifice the sacrifice, break the fast, or perform the Friday prayer."
"5139","(5139) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, who said: Masruq came out, and Urwah bin Al-Mughirah, and a group of Abdullah’s companions, attended the gathering but they did not gather, and the breaking of the fast came but they did not break the fast."
"5140","(5140) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah spent one or two winters in Kabul, not putting the congregation together, and praying two rak’ahs."
"5141","(5141) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Anas bin Malik stayed in Nisapur for a year or two, and he would pray two rak’ahs, then he would say the salaam, then he would pray. Two rak'ahs, then he says the salaam, but does not combine it."
"5142","(5142) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to wage war, and they would establish the Sunnah. Or something like that. They shorten the prayer, but do not join it together."
"5143","(5143) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Hisham bin al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, who said: Abd al-Malik bin Marwan wanted to pray in the Holy House, so he went to his room to stand in front of Abraham, so I met him and the soldiers, so I entered. Ali, and he said: O Your servants, we are a traveling people and it is not upon us to gather together, so gather with your companions."
"5144","(5144) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Zayd, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, he said : The Muslims are not obligated to unite them on their journey, nor on the day they disperse."
"5145","(5145) Zaid bin Hubab narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The traveler is not obligated to join the prayer."
"5146","(5146) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Raja’ bin Abi Salamah told us, he said: Abu Ubaid, Sulaiman’s servant, told me. Ibn Abdul-Malik, he said: Omar Ibn Abdul-Aziz left Dabiq, and he was the Commander of the Faithful at that time, and he passed through Aleppo that day. Gather, so he said to her princess: Gather, for we are on a journey."
"5147","(5147) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qais, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar said: The Friday prayer does not prevent one from travelling."
"5148","(5148) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan; That Abu Ubaidah went out on Friday on some of his travels, and he did not wait for the Friday prayer."
"5149","(5149) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’; A son of Saeed bin Zaid bin Nufayl was on land he owned in Al-Aqiq, at the head of a few miles from Medina, and he met Ibn Omar. He went to the Friday prayer and told him about his complaint, so he went to him and left the Friday prayer."
"5150","(5150) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in traveling on a Friday, unless The time for prayer comes."
"5151","(5151) Hushaym told us, saying: Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to say that."
"5152","(5152) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in traveling on Friday."
"5153","(5153) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Dhu’ib. He said: I went out with Al-Zubayr on Friday, and he led the Friday prayer for four."
"5154","(5154) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: I saw Ibn Shihab wanting to travel on Friday. At dawn, I said to him: Are you traveling on Friday? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, traveled on Friday. (Abu Dawud 310; Abd al-Razzaq 5540)"
"5155","(5155) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: If the crowd overtakes you, Do not go out until you have prayed the Friday prayer."
"5156","(5156) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; He was traveling on the night of Friday, so when dawn came he did not travel."
"5157","(5157) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythamiyah, he said: They used to prefer it if the congregation was present, or not. They will go out until they are gathered."
"5158","(5158) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, who said: If he travels on Friday He was called upon him; Not to be accompanied or helped during his travel. (Abdul Razzaq 5542)"
"5159","(5159) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of someone who heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab say: Traveling on Friday after Prayer"
"5160","(5160) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A people came out and the crowd was present, so a fire broke out. On them is a fire other than fire, which they will see."
"5161","(5161) Shazan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa; Urwa was traveling on Friday night, and was not waiting for Friday prayers."
"5162","(5162) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, he said: Sa’d used to speak. After Friday"
"5163","(5163) Bishr bin Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad, who said: We used to have lunch and have a nap after the Friday prayer. (Bukhari 9398 Muslim 588)"
"5164","(5164) Hushaym told us, he said: Muhammad bin Saad Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of his father, he said: We used to gather with Uthman bin Affan, then we will return and narrate."
"5165","(5165) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: We used to gather, then we would return and transfer. (Bukhari 940)"
"5166","(5166) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Thabit ibn al-Hajjaj narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: We used to gather, then we would come back and take a nap."
"5167","(5167) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Budail ibn Misra, on the authority of a woman, who said: I got along with Omar Sunnah, She said it after the Friday prayer."
"5168","(5168) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: We used to gather with Abu Wa’il, then we would come back and take a nap."
"5169","(5169) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Suwayd bin Ghafli, who said: We used to perform the Friday prayer, then we would return. We will talk about it"
"5170","(5170) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: We used to pray in congregation with Abdullah, then We will go back and have a nap."
"5171","(5171) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, he said: Our sheikhs narrated to us, among them: Abu Salamah, He said: We used to take a nap after the Friday prayer."
"5172","(5172) Abdullah bin Al-Ajlah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Al-Dhail say: We were We pray the Friday prayer, then we come back and have a nap."
"5173","(5173) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: People do not have a festival except at the beginning of the day."
"5174","(5174) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Thabit bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Kalabi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sidan. Al-Salami, he said: I witnessed the gathering with Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, and his sermon and prayer took place before noon, then we witnessed With Omar, his sermon and prayer were until I said: The middle of the day, then we witnessed with Othman, so his prayer was I engaged him until I said: The day has passed, but I did not see anyone criticizing that, nor denying it."
"5175","(5175) Jarir told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Those before you used to pray in congregation. And the Kaaba remained as it was."
"5176","(5176) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Salamah, he said: Abdullah led us in prayer. The crowd sacrificed, and said: I feared you would be burned."
"5177","(5177) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murr, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Suwayd, he said: Mu’awiyah led us in prayer. Friday is a sacrifice."
"5178","(5178) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Falih bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Othman bin Abdul Rahman told me; He heard Anas bin Malik say: We used to pray in congregation with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sun set. (Bukhari 904, Abu Dawud 1077)"
"5179","(5179) Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Hassan bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: We used to pray in congregation with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and then we would come back and clean our washing machines. Hassan said: So I said to Ja`far: What kind of messenger did you come to? He said: the noon of the sun. (Muslim 29)"
"5180","(5180) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa`, on the authority of his father, he said: We were We pray in congregation with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when the sun has passed the noon, then we return to follow the group. (Bukhār 4168, Muslim 32)"
"5181","(5181) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Anbas Amr ibn Marwan, on the authority of his father, who said: We used to gather with Ali when she passed away. The sun"
"5182","(5182) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Bilal al-Absi; Ammar led the people in prayer together, and the people were in two groups: some of them said: The sun has passed the setting, and some of them say: It has not passed."
"5183","(5183) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, who said: Muadh came to Mecca and they were gathering. In Al-Hijr, he said: Do not gather until the Ka’bah is turned from its face."
"5184","(5184) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: They used to perform the Friday prayer during the reign of Omar bin Abdul Aziz. And the Fay is Haniyah."
"5185","(5185) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The time for Friday prayer is at noon."
"5186","(5186) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Abu Razin, who said: We used to pray with Ali. Plural, sometimes we find a fa', and sometimes we do not find it."
"5187","(5187) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: Al-Nu’man ibn Bashir used to lead us in prayer. Friday after the sun has set."
"5188","(5188) Muhammad bin Bishr Al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah bin Al-Walid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Al-Aizar, he said: What I saw an imam who performed the Friday prayer better than Amr bin Harith. He used to lead it when the sun had passed the zenith."
"5189","(5189) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The time for the Friday prayer, the time for the noon prayer."
"5190","(5190) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of a client of the Al-Zubayr family. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Friday prayer is obligatory for every dreamer, except four: the child, the slave, And the woman, and the sick. (Bayhaqi 184)"
"5191","(5191) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b al-Qurazi, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: Whoever believes in God and the Last Day, then the Friday prayer is upon him, except upon a woman or a child. Or a slave, or a sick person."
"5192","(5192) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Women are not obligated to join them together."
"5193","(5193) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: I heard Al-Sha’abi say: The plural is a right upon me. Every believer, except three: a slave, a sick person, or a woman."
"5194","(5194) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Al-Wasafi, he said: I was with Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and he wrote to Abdul Al-Hamid: Look at the women before you. They will not attend a congregational prayer or a funeral, for they have no right to a congregational prayer, nor a funeral. Funeral"
"5195","(5195) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The servant is not obligated to do so."
"5196","(5196) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The servant is not obligated to join prayers."
"5197","(5197) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muslim bin Najih, on the authority of Abdullah bin Maadan, on the authority of his grandmother, she said: He told us Abdullah bin Masoud: If you pray on Friday with the imam, pray with his prayer, and if you pray in your homes Then pray four times."
"5198","(5198) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a woman who attends the mosque on Friday, she prays with the imam’s prayer, and that is sufficient for her."
"5199","(5199) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If two men are gathered together with the imam, that is sufficient for the imam’s prayer."
"5200","(5200) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The women used to have intercourse with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. And it was said: Do not go out except to spit, for there will not be a pleasant scent from you."
"5201","(5201) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the case of a woman coming in congregation, he said: She prays two rak’ahs and that is sufficient for her, but she is not allowed to come. Friday"
"5202","(5202) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The women of the immigrants used to perform the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. May God bless him and grant him peace. Then they will be called to account for it from the outward appearance."
"5203","(5203) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, who said: If she prays with the imam, that is sufficient."
"5204","(5204) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The companions of Al-Ghatfani and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He, peace and blessings be upon him, delivers a Friday sermon, and he said: Pray two rak’ahs, and you will complete them. (Bukhari 1166. Tirmidhi 510)"
"5205","(5205) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour, Abu Hurriyah, and Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He came to ask Al-Ghatfani and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving the Friday sermon, but he had not prayed the two rak’ahs, so he ordered him The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was required to pray two rak’ahs, during which he passed them."
"5206","(5206) Hushaym told us, saying: Abu Ma’shar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to pray two rak’ahs, he refrained from preaching until he finished. He prayed two rak'ahs, then returned to his sermon. (Daraqutni 13)"
"5207","(5207) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Abi Al-Darda’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was praying two rak'ahs while the imam was giving the sermon."
"5208","(5208) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Al-Hasan used to come while the imam was delivering the sermon and pray two rak’ahs."
"5209","(5209) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If you come while the imam is delivering the sermon on the day Friday, if you wish, you may kneel two rak’ahs, and if you wish, you may sit."
"5210","(5210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid (H) and on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith On the authority of Ali (H), on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; They disliked prayer while the imam was giving the Friday sermon."
"5211","(5211) Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to say: When the imam leaves, no one should pray until the imam finishes."
"5212","(5212) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: I saw a sect who entered on Friday from... Kinda doors, so he sat down and did not pray."
"5213","(5213) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: When the imam sits On the pulpit, there is no prayer."
"5214","(5214) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a man who comes on Friday and the imam is delivering the sermon, but he does not pray."
"5215","(5215) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Ibn Sirin used to sit and not pray."
"5216","(5216) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abu Malik Al-Qurazi said: I met Omar and Othman, and when the imam came out on the day of Friday prayer, we would abandon the prayer."
"5217","(5217) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Al-Musayyab, who said: The departure of the Imam will be cut off. Prayer"
"5218","(5218) Ibn Numair told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Omar; They both hated praying and speaking after the imam came out."
"5219","(5219) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Toubah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: He was a gentleman when he came. Friday prayers. If the imam did not go out, he prayed two rak’ahs, and if he did go out, he sat and hid himself, facing the imam, and did not turn around. To the right, not to the left."
"5220","(5220) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: It was the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Two sermons, between which he sits, recites the Qur’an and reminds the people. (Muslim 35. Abu Dawud 1087)"
"5221","(5221) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He delivers the sermon standing, then sits, then stands, delivering two sermons. (Bayhaqi 198)"
"5222","(5222) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Neither Abu Bakr nor Omar were sitting on the pulpit. On the day of Friday, and the first to sit with Muawiyah."
"5223","(5223) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech standing. Abu Bakr was standing, and Othman was standing, and the first to sit on the pulpit was Muawiyah bin Abi Sufyan."
"5224","(5224) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ishaq, who said: I saw Ali delivering a sermon on the pulpit, but he did not He sits until he is finished."
"5225","(5225) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra, he said: He entered the mosque and Abd al-Rahman bin Umm al-Hakam was delivering the sermon sitting, so he said: Look at this young man delivering the sermon while sitting. God Almighty said: (And when they see your merchants, or they turn away, they disperse to it and leave you standing.)"
"5226","(5226) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: A man asked him, “Would the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace?” Does God, may God bless him and grant him peace, deliver the sermon standing or sitting? He said: Didn't you read: {And they left you standing}"
"5227","(5227) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A caravan came with its trade on the day of Friday. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon, so the people left to watch, and the Messenger of God remained with twelve men. Then these verses were revealed: {And when they saw your merchants, or their amusements, they dispersed to it and left you standing}"
"5228","(5228) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Sitting on the pulpit on Friday is an invitation."
"5229","(5229) Ahmad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: Al-Mughirah used to deliver a sermon. He was standing in congregation, and there was only one muezzin."
"5230","(5230) Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Hassan bin Salih told us, on the authority of Simak, he said: I saw Al-Nu’man giving a sermon. Standing"
"5231","(5231) Shababi bin Siwar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Salih, he said: I saw Abu Hurairah, Marwan had appointed him as his successor in charge of Medina, and he would deliver two sermons and sit for two sessions."
"5232","(5232) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. And he greeted; He used to deliver the Friday sermon standing, then sit, then get up and deliver the sermon. (Ahmad 1/257 Bazzar 640)"
"5233","(5233) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah was asked about the engagement on the day Friday? So he recited: {And they left you standing}"
"5234","(5234) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I asked Abu Ubaidah about the sermon on the day Friday? So he recited: {And they left you standing}"
"5235","(5235) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He was asked about the Prophet’s sermon, may God bless him and grant him peace, on Friday? So he recited: {And they left you standing}"
"5236","(5236) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: Mu’awiyah only delivered the speech while sitting, when his belly fat increased. And his flesh"
"5237","(5237) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amri told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver two sermons, sitting between them. (Bukhari 928 and Muslim 589)"
"5238","(5238) Abu Asama told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was when He ascended the pulpit on Friday, greeted the people, and said: Peace be upon you, and praise be to God and praise be to Him. He recites a surah, then sits, then gets up and delivers the sermon, then comes down. Abu Bakr and Omar were doing it. (Abdul Razzaq 5281)"
"5239","(5239) Ghassan bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, who said: Othman had grown old, so when He ascended the pulpit, ascended the ladder, and continued for as long as a human being would read the book."
"5240","(5240) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir; When Omar bin Abdul Aziz sat on the pulpit, he would greet the people and they would respond to him."
"5241","(5241) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: The sermons of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were He greeted intentionally, and his prayer was intentional."
"5242","(5242) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Abdullah said: The shortness of the sermon and the length of the prayer is a sin. From the jurisprudence of a man. (Bazzar 638)"
"5243","(5243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: Abdullah said: Perform this prayer well, and shorten it. This is the sermon."
"5244","(5244) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Salih, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, he said: Abu Rashid narrated to us, he said: He addressed us. Ammar, then he continued his speech, and a man said: You have said something that would be good, if only you had been at length. So he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he forbade us from prolonging the sermon. (Abu Dawud 1099, Hakim 289)"
"5245","(5245) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of Yahya Bin Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Saad bin Zurara, on the authority of Umm Hisham, the son of my neighbor, or Harith, who said: What I learned (the Qur’an and the Glorious Qur’an) only on the tongue of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, reciting it to the people every day. All together when he addresses them. (Muslim 51, Abu Dawud 1093)"
"5246","(5246) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, who said: Omar used to like He recites Surah Al Imran in congregation when he delivers the sermon."
"5247","(5247) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Harun bin Antarah, on the authority of his father; That Ali recited while he was on the pulpit: {Say, O disbelievers} and {Say: He is Allah, One}."
"5248","(5248) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abu Abd al-Rahman, who said: We camped in al-Mada’in, and were among them. At the head of a farsakh, the group came, so my father came and I came with him, so Hudhayfah addressed us, and he said: Indeed, God is Blessed and Most High. He says: {The Hour has approached and the moon has split open}"
"5249","(5249) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Bakr ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Safwan ibn Mahrez, he said: Al-Ash’ari is among us. He delivers the Friday sermon, when he recited the last prostration in Surah Al-Hajj."
"5250","(5250) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz reciting while he was on the pulpit: {And turn in repentance to your Lord and submit to Him}, and in His hand is a staff."
"5251","(5251) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Simak ibn Harb, who said: I said to him: How were Nu’man’s speeches? He said: He was shining with his hands. He said: Al-Dahhak bin Qais used to join his hand when he delivered a sermon."
"5252","(5252) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amara bin Ruwaibi; He saw Bishr bin Marwan raising his hands on the pulpit and said: May God bless these hands. I have seen the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said nothing more than that with his hand like this, and pointed the rosary with his finger. (Tirmidhi 515, Abu Dawud 1097)"
"5253","(5253) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The imam’s permission on the day of the congregational prayer is He gestures with his hand."
"5254","(5254) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They used to ask the Imam for permission, and he... On the pulpit, when Ziyad was present and this was increasing, he said: Whoever puts his hand on his nose, it is his ear."
"5255","(5255) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The companions of Al-Ghatfani and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He, peace and blessings be upon him, was giving the Friday sermon, and he said to him: Did you pray? He said: No, he said: Pray two rak'ahs, complete them both."
"5256","(5256) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to deliver a sermon, and he said: To the people: Sit down. Abdullah bin Masoud heard him while he was at the door, so he sat down and said to him: O Abdullah, come in. (Abdul Razzaq 5368. Bayhaqi 218)"
"5257","(5257) Issa bin Yunus and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Qays, who said: My father came The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was giving a sermon, so he stood in front of him in the sun, so he commanded that it be done, so it was turned into the shadow. (Ahmad 3/426 Hakim 171)"
"5258","(5258) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: They used to greet the imam while he was on the pulpit and he would respond."
"5259","(5259) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hilal ibn Qays, on the authority of Zayd ibn Suhan, who said: Then I heard the man and the imam speaking on Friday. If he is close to you, wink at him, and if he is far away, point. To Him, and do not throw pebbles at Him."
"5260","(5260) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Layla and he pointed to Muhammad ibn Saad, and he spoke: to be silent."
"5261","(5261) Ibn Numayr told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw a man speaking while the imam was giving the Friday sermon, so he threw pebbles at him, and when he looked at him, he put his hand on them. Therein"
"5262","(5262) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; Concerning a man speaking while the imam was giving a Friday sermon, and he said: He should put his hand on his mouth and not throw pebbles at him."
"5263","(5263) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He places his hand on it."
"5264","(5264) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; He was indicating to the man who was speaking to be silent."
"5265","(5265) Hushaym told us, he said: Some of our sheikhs told us about Al-Hasan; He saw a man speaking on Friday while the imam was giving the sermon, so he threw pebbles at him."
"5266","(5266) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Do not point to Sunday, Friday, and do not forbid anything, and do not supplicate except for the Imam to supplicate."
"5267","(5267) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Majza’ ibn Zahir, on the authority of his father; He saw a man speaking on Friday, so he motioned to him to be silent."
"5268","(5268) Shababah bin Siwar told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdullah bin Yasar, who said: I was With Saeed bin Jubayr on Friday while the imam was delivering the sermon. I touched the pebbles and my hand hit me."
"5269","(5269) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajlili, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace When he delivered a sermon, his companions would receive him with great joy. (Ibn Majah 1136)"
"5270","(5270) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih; He used to face the Imam on the Friday sermon when he delivered a sermon, and he would not say such-and-such or such-and-such."
"5271","(5271) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; About the one who saw Sa`sa`a facing the imam on the day of Friday prayer."
"5272","(5272) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is Sunnah to greet the imam on the day of Friday prayer."
"5273","(5273) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: I saw Al-Nadr bin Anas receiving the Imam."
"5274","(5274) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, he said: I saw Abraham on the day of Friday entering from the gates of Canada. So he sat down and made his face towards the pulpit."
"5275","(5275) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Wasil bin Al-Sa’ib Al-Raqqashi, who said: I saw Ata, a peacock, and a mujahid greeting us. Imam on Friday."
"5276","(5276) Abd Al-Samad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mustamir bin Al-Rayyan, who said: I saw a man at the first gate on the day of the Friday prayer. The pulpit"
"5277","(5277) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, and Al-Qasim; They used to receive the Imam on Friday prayers."
"5278","(5278) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim bin Daylam, on the authority of Zazan; He used to receive the imam on Friday prayers."
"5279","(5279) Hushaym told us, he said: Abdul Hamid bin Jafar Al-Ansari told us, with a chain of transmission that I do not remember, he said: They were They come on Friday and sit around the pulpit, then they approach the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. With their faces"
"5280","(5280) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz, he said: The preacher Before him, meaning the Imam."
"5281","(5281) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He was hiding while the imam was giving the sermon."
"5282","(5282) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He was hiding on Friday while the imam was giving the sermon."
"5283","(5283) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, who said: I saw Salim and al-Qasim Huttibayan on the day of Friday prayer. And the imam is delivering the sermon."
"5284","(5284) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Fitr, who said: I saw a person giving in hiding on the day of Friday."
"5285","(5285) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I saw Al-Hasan hiding while the Imam was giving the Friday sermon."
"5286","(5286) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Salem Al-Khayyat, who said: I saw Al-Hasan, Muhammad, and Ikrimah bin Khaled. Al-Makhzoumi, Amr bin Dinar, Abu Al-Zubayr, and Ata’ were celebrating the Friday sermon while the imam was giving the sermon."
"5287","(5287) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to hide while the imam was giving the Friday sermon."
"5288","(5288) Abu Usama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar used to watch you on the day of Friday. And the imam is delivering the sermon."
"5289","(5289) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhul, Ata’, and Al-Hasan; They hated to join in prayer while the imam was delivering the Friday sermon."
"5290","(5290) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I heard a man giving a sermon, saying, Muhammad said: Sleep in The plural is from Satan, so if any of you feels sleepy, let him turn away."
"5291","(5291) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: If you fall asleep on the day of Friday prayer and the imam is giving the sermon So he transformed."
"5292","(5292) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, who said: Muhammad used to wake up the sleeping person on the day of Friday prayer, and the imam would deliver the sermon."
"5293","(5293) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; If he was afraid that he would fall asleep during the Friday prayer, he would turn away."
"5294","(5294) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos; About the one who is sleepy on Friday, and one of them said: He will move from his place, and the other said: He will move from his place."
"5295","(5295) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Sleeping, or drowsiness. On Friday, it is from Satan, so if one of you slumbers, let him turn away."
"5296","(5296) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: If one of you feels sleepy on the day of Friday, let him move from his seat to another. (Tirmidhi 526, Abu Dawud 112)"
"5297","(5297) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Because the whips are different on my back, I love it more than sleeping while the imam is giving the Friday sermon."
"5298","(5298) Ismail bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri; That Abu Al-Alaa used to sleep on Friday while sitting."
"5299","(5299) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdullah ibn al-Mukhtar, on the authority of Malik ibn Dinar, who said: Abu Al-Aliyah and Khalas bin Amr slept for a long time on Friday, then they got up and prayed."
"5300","(5300) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hurriya, on the authority of Nafi’ He said: Ibn Umar used to hunker down on Friday while the imam was giving the sermon, and if he took a long time, he would put his head on my lap."
"5301","(5301) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to greet him when he came while the imam was delivering a sermon, and they would return his greeting."
"5302","(5302) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah, and Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: They used to return the greeting on the Day of Resurrection. Friday prayer while the imam is delivering the sermon, and they gloat at the sneezing person."
"5303","(5303) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; Concerning a man entering the mosque on the day of Friday and the imam had come out and said: “He should greet him” and they would respond to him, and if he sneezed they would curse him and respond. Aliyah"
"5304","(5304) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Salem, who said: The greeting of the greeting is returned on Friday. And he hears you."
"5305","(5305) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abu Awani, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus; He hated to return the greeting and gloat at someone who sneezed while the imam was delivering the sermon."
"5306","(5306) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Ibn Sirin; That he asked them about returning the greeting on Friday while the imam was giving the sermon? They said: It used to be said: Whoever says, “Listen,” has negligently negated."
"5307","(5307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Silence."
"5308","(5308) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Muhammad used to say: If he greets you on the day of the Friday prayer and the imam is delivering the sermon So I gestured to him."
"5309","(5309) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, who said: I heard Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and a man asked him about a man who smelled a man. And the imam is giving the sermon, he canceled it? He said: No, but he will not come back."
"5310","(5310) Waki` told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Muhammad ibn Ali said, and al-Qasim: He refers to himself."
"5311","(5311) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: I greeted Ibrahim while the imam was delivering the sermon. On the day of Friday, he did not answer me, and he said when he prayed: Speech is disliked."
"5312","(5312) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; A prince in Bahrain complained, so he ordered a man to lead the people in prayer, but he did not deliver a sermon, so he prayed four. Muhammad said: So he followed the Sunnah."
"5313","(5313) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Like him"
"5314","(5314) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the imam does not deliver the sermon, he will pray. Four"
"5315","(5315) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If the imam does not deliver a sermon, he prays four times."
"5316","(5316) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ told us, he said: I heard Ibn Tawus He mentioned this, on the authority of his father, who said: Whoever delivers the sermon, let him pray two rak’ahs, and whoever does not deliver the sermon, let him pray four."
"5317","(5317) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He used to pray four times."
"5318","(5318) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: He prays four times."
"5319","(5319) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He set out on Hajj and came to Tabuk on Friday, and their imam prayed two rak’ahs, but he did not deliver a sermon. Makhoul said: May God fight this man who shortened the people’s prayer and did not deliver the sermon. Rather, the congregational prayer was shortened for the sake of the sermon."
"5320","(5320) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of his father; When the imam delivered the sermon, he did not say tasbih or supplicate."
"5321","(5321) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Maimun; He hated speaking while the imam was giving the Friday sermon, and he said: He remembers God."
"5322","(5322) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If the imam speaks on the day of Friday prayer, then there is no speech except He recites the Qur’an."
"5323","(5323) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I said to your scholars: Should I recite within myself? He said: Perhaps that is so that there is no harm in it."
"5324","(5324) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a man on the day of Friday prayer to mention God to himself while the imam was giving the sermon."
"5325","(5325) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Muhammad about a man who was far away from the crowd on Friday. The imam, who cannot hear his voice, recites in his companion’s ear? He said: I do not know that it is wrong for a man to mention God to himself."
"5326","(5326) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in reciting and remembering God. If they read the newspapers on Friday."
"5327","(5327) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: There is no harm in talking while the pages are read on Friday."
"5328","(5328) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith; Abu Burda used to speak in congregation while the newspapers were being read, but Al-Sha’bi did not see anything wrong with him."
"5329","(5329) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, he said: There is no problem. By speaking when the newspapers are read on Friday, until the imam takes the sermon."
"5330","(5330) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; He forbade newspapers from being read on Friday until he finished sermons."
"5331","(5331) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: I said to Abraham: Indeed, the Scriptures come before... My book contains falsehood and lies, so if I want to speak to my friend or listen? He said: No, but listen, meaning in congregation."
"5332","(5332) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Hammad bin Abi Suleiman told me while the muezzins were calling the call to prayer. On the day of Friday, the imam came out and spoke to me, but I did not speak to him. Then we gathered in another gathering, and he spoke to me while the newspapers were being read, so he began to speak to me, and I would not speak to him, so he said: My brother’s son, The silence was only before the day when they were preached about the Book of God and said about it, so we kept silent because of this message of theirs?"
"5333","(5333) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Speech was disliked and the pages were read, and Al-Hasan said: The newspapers were read before prayer."
"5334","(5334) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Khaled bin Issa, he said: I saw Omar bin Abd Al-Aziz Al-Walid bin Hisham and Sulaiman, the Commander of the Faithful, speak on the pulpit, and newspapers are read on Friday."
"5335","(5335) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Enough idle talk then. The imam ascended the pulpit. You must tell your friend to listen."
"5336","(5336) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I said to your scholars: When will speech be disliked on the Day of Resurrection? Friday? He said: When the Imam ascends the pulpit, and when the Imam delivers a sermon, and when the Imam speaks."
"5337","(5337) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever says to his companion on the day of Friday: “Be silent while the imam is giving the sermon,” has negated. (Abdul Razzaq 5417)"
"5338","(5338) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zinad, on the authority of al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: If you say Listen to your friend, for you have deviated eloquently."
"5339","(5339) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah, on the authority of Tha’labah bin Abu Malik Al-Qurazi said: I met Omar and Othman, and when the imam came out on the day of Friday prayer, we left the prayer. He spoke, we left talking."
"5340","(5340) Ibn Numair told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Omar; They both hated praying and speaking on Friday after the Imam appeared."
"5341","(5341) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray on Friday, but when the imam left, he did not pray."
"5342","(5342) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Al-Musayyab, who said: The imam’s departure interrupts the prayer. And his words interrupt speech."
"5343","(5343) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Maimoon bin Mihran; He hated speaking while the imam was giving sermons."
"5344","(5344) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The imam’s appearance interrupts the prayer, and his speech interrupts the prayer. Speech"
"5345","(5345) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: If a man says on the day of Friday prayer while the imam is delivering the sermon, listen, then he has negated."
"5346","(5346) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Alqamah bin Abd God, he said: We came to Medina on Friday, so I ordered my companions to leave, then I came to the mosque, and I sat near Ibn Umar, then a man from my companions came and started speaking to me while the imam was giving the sermon. We did such-and-such, and when he continued, I said to him: Be quiet. When we finished the prayer, I mentioned that to Ibn Omar, and he said: As for you, there is no plural of it for you, and as for your companion, he is a donkey."
"5347","(5347) Hushaym told us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; That Abu Dharr, or Al-Zubair bin Al-Awwam, one of them heard a verse from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, which he recited while he was on The pulpit on Friday. He said: Then he said to his companion: When were these verses revealed? He said: When he finished his prayer, Omar bin Al-Khattab said to him: No, you have no choice but to do so. So he came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and mentioned That is for him. He said: So he said: Omar spoke the truth."
"5348","(5348) Ibn Numair told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever speaks on Friday while the imam is delivering the sermon is like a donkey carrying books, and the one who tells him to listen is not May God have mercy on you (Ahmad 1/230)"
"5349","(5349) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: Sa’d said to a man on the day of Friday prayer: No prayer. For you, he said: Then that man mentioned that to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: O Messenger of God, Sa’d said: No blessings for you. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Why, Saad? He said: He spoke while you were giving the sermon, and he said: Saad spoke the truth. (Bazzar 642, Abu Ali 708)"
"5350","(5350) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Saksaki, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Awfa, who said: Three Whoever is spared from them will be forgiven for what is between him and the other group. For him to do something that does not mean harm from his heart, or to speak, or to say: “Shout.”"
"5351","(5351) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hariri, who said: When he said, “On the Day of Friday prayers while the imam is delivering the sermon: “Saha”, it has been cancelled."
"5352","(5352) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ismail bin Abi Khaled told us, he said: I saw Abraham talking to a man And the imam delivers the Friday sermon."
"5353","(5353) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Urwah bin Al-Zubayr, he said: It was He sees no harm in speaking if he does not hear the Friday sermon."
"5354","(5354) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw Ibrahim and Sa`id bin Jubayr and Al-Hajjaj are talking, and Al-Hajjaj is giving a sermon."
"5355","(5355) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Burd ibn Sinan, on the authority of Az-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Perhaps he spoke about Hajj on the day of Friday, in between his coming down from his pulpit to his prayer place. (Abu Dawud 63)"
"5356","(5356) Yahya bin Sulaym al-Taifi told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I met my father and those who passed away from among them. May His satisfaction and We take it from them. They see no harm in speaking when the imam comes down from the pulpit until he begins the prayer."
"5357","(5357) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, who said: A peacock spoke to me after Suleiman descended from the The pulpit"
"5358","(5358) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; Indeed, they did not see any harm in him speaking during his revelation until he said “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5359","(5359) Hushaym told us, saying: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in speaking until he gave the sermon, and when he finished the sermon until he entered into the prayer."
"5360","(5360) Waki` told us, on the authority of Shu`bai, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about speaking when the imam goes out to speak. And if he came down before he prayed? The arbitrator disapproved of it, and Hammad said: There is no harm in it."
"5361","(5361) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of his followers, who said: He speaks as long as he does not sit."
"5362","(5362) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was On Friday, when he said the salaam, he would come down from the pulpit, and the man would stand with him and talk to him about the matter, then he would go to He prayed and he prayed. (Tirmidhi 517 and Abu Dawud 1113)"
"5363","(5363) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Ibrahim, and Ibrahim bin Muhajir They were talking on Friday while the imam was delivering the sermon, so I met Ibrahim bin Muhajir after that, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: We used to pray. The imam was Al-Hajjaj."
"5364","(5364) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It was said: There is no speech after the imam descends from the throne. The pulpit until the prayer is finished."
"5365","(5365) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I was informed on the authority of Abraham that he hated him."
"5366","(5366) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Ibn al-Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Ibn Ulaathah, on the authority of Al-Zahri; Concerning the one who speaks while the imam is delivering the Friday sermon, they said: He prays two rak’ahs."
"5367","(5367) Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: It was narrated on the authority of Omar ibn al-Khattab that he said: The sermon is only made in place of the two rak’ahs, so if the sermon does not follow Let him pray four times."
"5368","(5368) Hushaym told us, saying: Dawud bin Abi Hind told us, on the authority of Ata’; He used to say: If he does not reach the sermon, let him pray four times."
"5369","(5369) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata, a peacock, and Mujahid; They said: If he misses the Friday sermon, he should pray four times."
"5370","(5370) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: He told me about Ata’ and Tawoos, they said: Whoever missed the stories on the day of Friday prayer. Let him pray four times."
"5371","(5371) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If he misses the sermon, he prays four times."
"5372","(5372) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa ibn Abd al-Wahid al-Ramli, who said: I heard Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, He said: If he misses the sermon, let him pray four times."
"5373","(5373) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: The saying of the people of Mecca was mentioned to Muhammad, if the When he reached the sermon, he prayed four times and said: “This is nothing.”"
"5374","(5374) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, he said: The gathering was Four, so two rak'ahs were made for the sermon, so whoever missed the sermon should pray four."
"5375","(5375) Hushaym told us, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zayd informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said : Abdullah said: Whoever catches up with one rak’ah of the Friday prayer, let him pray another, and whoever does not catch up with the kneeling, let him pray four."
"5376","(5376) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: Abdullah said: Who has brought you together? It is two rak'ahs, and whoever does not realize it, let him pray four."
"5377","(5377) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Who among the crowd recognized you? One rak'ah, let him add another to it."
"5378","(5378) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abu Muammar said: Something I wished I had I asked about the lions. He said: Abraham said: What is it? Perhaps you have had enough of it. He said: The man standing up from the crowd in a rak’ah? He said: Al-Aswad said: Whoever of the congregation catches up with one rak’ah should pray another rak’ah, and whoever does not catch up with the bowing should pray another rak’ah. Four"
"5379","(5379) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus informed us, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: Whoever misses one rak’ah from the congregation should add another to it, and whoever does not miss it should add another to it. When bowing, let him pray four times."
"5380","(5380) Hushaym told us, he said: Ismail bin Salem told us, he said: I heard Al-Sha’abi say: Whoever realizes the sermon It is the Friday prayer, and whoever performs two rak’ahs has performed the Friday prayer, and whoever performs two rak’ahs has performed the congregation, so let him pray. Another rak'ah, and whoever does not know how to perform the rak'ah, let him pray four."
"5381","(5381) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever does not know how to bow On Friday, let him pray four times."
"5382","(5382) Hushaym told us, he said: Sa’id told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab; They both said: Whoever performs a rak'ah from the congregation, let him perform another rak'ah."
"5383","(5383) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad, who said: When he catches up, bow down. From the plural, he added another word to it."
"5384","(5384) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Al-Qamah, they said: When you catch up with the crowd rak'ah, then add another rak'ah to it."
"5385","(5385) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Whoever performs a rak’ah of yours, let him add another rak’ah to it. Other"
"5386","(5386) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: When he performs a rak’ah from the congregation, he prays To another way."
"5387","(5387) Khaled bin Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, who said: I said to Maymun: Have you performed a rak’ah from the congregation? He said: As for me, I was building what remained."
"5388","(5388) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say: Whoever missed a rak’ah of Friday prayer, let him pray another rak’ah, and whoever does not catch it, let him pray four."
"5389","(5389) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: When you perform a rak’ah, add another to it."
"5390","(5390) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Salim, he said: When someone overtakes you, The Friday prayer is a rak'ah and he added another rak'ah to it."
"5391","(5391) Ishaq al-Razi told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of al-Qasim; Salim said: If I had not left you except one rak’ah of Friday prayer, I would have added another rak’ah to it."
"5392","(5392) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, Anas, and Al-Hasan, they said: When he joins the congregation, he performs a raka’ah and adds another to it, and when he joins them sitting, he prays four times."
"5393","(5393) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Alqamiya and al-Aswad, They said: When he meets them sitting, he prays four times."
"5394","(5394) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: If he comes while the imam is sitting on the day of Friday prayer? He said: He prays four times."
"5395","(5395) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He prays four times."
"5396","(5396) Abdou told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, he said: When he reaches you on the day of Friday Sitting, he prayed four times."
"5397","(5397) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id, Khallas, Al-Hasan (h) and on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"5398","(5398) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who comes on the day of Jumu’ah before the Does the imam greet? They said: He prays two rak'ahs."
"5399","(5399) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, he said: When the people arrive on the day of Friday Sitting, he prayed two rak'ahs."
"5400","(5400) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He prays. Two rak'ahs"
"5401","(5401) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Aamir bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Abu Wael, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever realizes tash-hud has attained it. Prayer"
"5402","(5402) It was narrated by Ibn Fudail, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: He used to pray before Friday is four."
"5403","(5403) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to perform the Hajj on Friday, So he prolongs the prayer before the imam comes out."
"5404","(5404) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Othman, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: Pray ten rak’ahs before the congregational prayer."
"5405","(5405) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to pray four times before it. (Tirmidhi 478) Ahmad 3/411)"
"5406","(5406) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He used to pray two rak'ahs in his house on Fridays."
"5407","(5407) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He did not come to the mosque on Friday until he had prayed two rak'ahs in his house."
"5408","(5408) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray two rak’ahs after the Friday prayer. (Bukhari 1145. Tirmidhi 521)"
"5409","(5409) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid bin Hilal, on the authority of Imran bin hippocampus; He was praying two rak'ahs after the Friday prayer, and it was said to him: O Abu Najaid, what are the people saying? He said: What do they say? He said: They say: You pray two rak'ahs to the Friday prayer, so it becomes four. He said: Imran said: For meteorites to fall between my ribs is more beloved to me than for me to do that. When it was the next Friday prayer, he prayed the Friday prayer, then hid himself and did not pray anything until the afternoon prayer was performed."
"5410","(5410) Hushaym told us, he said: Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, he said: Ibn Masoud came to us, He used to command us to pray four times after the Friday prayer, so when Ali came to us, he ordered us to pray six times, so we took Ali’s word. We left out the statement of Abdullah. He said: He used to pray two rak’ahs, then four."
"5411","(5411) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, who said: Abdullah was praying four times, when Ali came and prayed six rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and four rak'ahs."
"5412","(5412) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar prayed the congregational prayer, he would pray after it. Six rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, then four."
"5413","(5413) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa, on the authority of his father; He used to pray six rak'ahs after the Friday prayer."
"5414","(5414) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: He used to pray after the Friday prayer. Six rak'ahs, two rak'ahs, and four rak'ahs."
"5415","(5415) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Pray two rak’ahs after the Friday prayer, then pray After them, whatever you want."
"5416","(5416) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Sulaym, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever of you prays after the Friday prayer, let him pray four times. (Tirmidhi 523, Abu Dawud 1124)"
"5417","(5417) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Habib, who said: Abdullah was praying after Friday is four."
"5418","(5418) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to pray four times after the Friday prayer."
"5419","(5419) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah used to pray after Friday is four."
"5420","(5420) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah; He used to pray four rak'ahs after the Friday prayer, without separating between them."
"5421","(5421) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abu Husayn, who said: I saw Al-Aswad bin Yazid praying after the Friday prayer. Four"
"5422","(5422) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to pray four times after it."
"5423","(5423) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: If the imam says salaam, he prays two rak’ahs on the day of Friday prayer. And when he returns, he prays two rak'ahs."
"5424","(5424) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Hammad, who said: It was recommended in the following four days. The congregation does not say salaam between them."
"5425","(5425) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utba, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah; He used to pray four times after the Friday prayer."
"5426","(5426) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Kulthum ibn Jabr, who said: Muslim ibn Yassar said to me: If you knew that the Fire had It is the middle of the day of Friday, so do not buy anything."
"5427","(5427) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib; Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to prevent people from selling goods on Friday when prayer was called."
"5428","(5428) Hushaym told us, he said: Juwaybir told us, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, he said: If the sun has passed the zenith on the day of Friday, then Buying and selling is forbidden until the prayer is completed."
"5429","(5429) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and some of his companions, on the authority of Al-Hasan; They both said that."
"5430","(5430) Hushaym told us, saying: Abu Al-Miqdam, a client of Quraysh, told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad; He bought something from a man on the day of Friday, and he met him after that and said: Leave the sale to me, for I am of the same mind. I bought from you what I bought after sunrise."
"5431","(5431) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, or someone else, who said: Whoever sells something after When the sun has reached noon on Friday, then selling it will be returned, because God has forbidden selling if the call to prayer is made on the day of Friday"
"5432","(5432) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Burd, he said: I said to Al-Zuhari: When is it forbidden to buy and sell on Friday? He said: The call to prayer was when the imam came out, so the Commander of the Faithful, Othman, gave the third call to prayer, and he called the call to prayer to the visitors. For the people to come together, I think that buying and selling should be abandoned at the time of the call to prayer."
"5433","(5433) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Maimun, who said: He was in Medina when he gave the call to prayer. The muezzin on Friday calls out in the markets: It is forbidden to sell, it is forbidden to sell."
"5434","(5434) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; In the hour that is expected in congregation, he said: While he made it clear that the sale is forbidden until it is permissible."
"5435","(5435) Hushaym told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit; He went to the congregation, and behold, the people met him and prayed. He said: So he turned to a mosque, or to a house, and prayed. He said: So he was told about that? He said: He who is not ashamed before people is not ashamed before God."
"5436","(5436) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, and Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to say: If people meet you on the day of Friday prayer and they have prayed, go to the mosque, if you know what was recited with it. Imam, so recite and pray."
"5437","(5437) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; That Zayd bin Thabit found people returning from the gathering, so he went to a house, and it was said to him? He said: He who is not ashamed before people is not ashamed before God. He said: Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin said: He will continue."
"5438","(5438) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Muslim, who said: I witnessed Ibrahim al-Taymi and Ibrahim al-Nakha’i. Zur, and Ibn Kuhayl handed him over, so Zur and Al-Taymimi mentioned it on the day of Jumu’ah, then they prayed the congregational prayer for four days. Their place, and they were afraid."
"5439","(5439) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: A muezzin called the call to prayer while we were with the spirits on the day of Jumu’ah, so we came and they had prayed. Al-Qasim prayed but did not join in prayer."
"5440","(5440) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a people who missed the Friday prayer, he said: They pray in different ways."
"5441","(5441) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Al-Walid, he said: Ali said: There is no congregational prayer on the day of congregational prayer except with the Imam."
"5442","(5442) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Jamil bin Ubaid Al-Tai narrated to us, saying: I saw Iyas bin Muawiyah, and he At that time, the judge of Basra came to the Friday prayer and she missed it, so he came forward and led us in the noon prayer with four rak’ahs."
"5443","(5443) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, who said: I came to the mosque under heavy burden. Friday, and we found them praying, so we prayed together."
"5444","(5444) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Mukhtar Abi Ghassan, on the authority of Abi Dhabyan al-Janabi, who said: Ali said: The collection is given. Even if they crawl."
"5445","(5445) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Maymun bin Abi Shabib, who said: I wanted to combine it in The time of the pilgrims, so I prepared to go, then I said: Where should I go and pray behind this person? He said: So I said to one person: I will go, and another time: I will not go. He said: Then my two minds agreed on me going. He said: Then a caller called me from a side. The verse: {O you who have believed, when the call is made to prayer on the day of Friday, then strive to the remembrance of God and leave sale}"
"5446","(5446) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Hudhayl, he said: Remember the congregation. The time of Mukhtar, and he said: Bring her even if the water reaches pebbles."
"5447","(5447) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah bin Rawahi used to come. The congregation is walking, and when he returns, he returns however he wishes, if he wishes, walking, and if he wishes, riding."
"5448","(5448) Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Al-Walid bin Abi narrated to me. Al-Walid said: I saw Abu Hurairah walking to the gathering from Dhul-Halif."
"5449","(5449) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to hate it. Riding to Friday prayers and Eid prayers."
"5450","(5450) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade one’s face to be shaved to speak on the day of Friday prayer before the prayer."
"5451","(5451) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Yusuf bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib, he said: We were flying one day. Friday prayer before prayer."
"5452","(5452) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahariyyah, he said: I was with Abdullah bin On the day of Friday prayer, he continued speaking to me until the imam came out."
"5453","(5453) My grandfather Abu Amer Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Hilal, on the authority of his father, who said: Abu Hurairah was He will speak to us on Friday until the imam appears."
"5454","(5454) Zaid bin Hubab told us, he said: Al-Dahhak bin Othman told us, he said: Nafi’ told me, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to sit high and level in his assembly on the day of Friday before the imam came out."
"5455","(5455) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Qunoot on the day of Friday prayer is an invocation."
"5456","(5456) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He hated performing Qunoot on Friday."
"5457","(5457) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Sustenance in congregation is an invocation."
"5458","(5458) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I prayed behind Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba. Al-Numan bin Bashir was the one who did not perform the prayer, but he succeeded Ali. So I said: Is it true to you? He said: No."
"5459","(5459) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, he said: My father told me, he said: I met the people before Omar bin Abdul Aziz. They recite the Qunoot in the Jum’ah, but when the time of Omar bin Abdul Aziz came, the Qunoot in the Jum’ah was abandoned."
"5460","(5460) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: He was not a slave. Allah Ibn Umar recited Qunoot at Fajr and Friday."
"5461","(5461) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; It was desirable for the imam to enter when he prayed."
"5462","(5462) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Halhala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; When the congregation prayed and said the salutations, he would enter."
"5463","(5463) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace, he prays the two rak’ahs after the Friday prayer in his house."
"5464","(5464) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Qalab, who said: I prayed in congregation with him, and when I finished my prayer He took my hand, stood in my place, and put me in his place."
"5465","(5465) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Ad-Distawai, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kairir, who said: I saw Uqba bin Abdul Ghafir and Hassan bin Bilal on Friday, when the imam finished his prayer, they moved from their place."
"5466","(5466) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: Du’ama bin Yazid Al-Anbari narrated to me; He prayed alongside Abu Majlis in Friday prayer, and when the prayer was finished, he took my hand and made me stand in his place. He was in it, and he stood in my position."
"5467","(5467) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Habib, who said: I prayed next to Safwan ibn Mahrez Combined, so he changed me to his place, and he changed in my place."
"5468","(5468) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman told us, he said: Ata told us, he said: I saw Ibn Umar. He prayed in congregation, then he moved away from his place and prayed two rak’ahs, in which he prayed lightly, then he moved away from that place and prayed. Four, it is longer than your fig."
"5469","(5469) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Omar bin Ata bin Abi Al-Khawar informed me; Nafi’ bin Jubayr sent him to Al-Sa’ib, Nimr’s nephew, to ask him about something that Mu’awiyah had seen during prayer. He said: Yes, I prayed with him in congregation in the shrine. When the imam greeted, I stood in his place and prayed. When he entered, he sent for me and said: Do not repeat what you did. If you prayed the Friday prayer, do not continue it with a prayer until you have spoken or left, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, commanded us to do so: not to lead a prayer until we have spoken or gone out. (Muslim 73. Abu Dawud 122)"
"5470","(5470) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Sulaiman ibn Musa, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, he said: He hated it. Prayer is half the day, except on Friday."
"5471","(5471) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: On the day of Friday prayer, the whole prayer is performed."
"5472","(5472) Ali bin Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: It is disliked to pray at midday, except on the day of Friday."
"5473","(5473) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Mu’awiyah bin Qurayh about prayer before the sun goes down on the day of Friday? He did not see any harm in it."
"5474","(5474) Muhammad bin Musaar told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is disliked to pray at midday, except on Friday."
"5475","(5475) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: On the day of Friday prayer, the whole prayer is performed."
"5476","(5476) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in praying on Friday at midday."
"5477","(5477) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: The first call is on the day of Friday prayer; That which occurs when the imam emerges, and that which occurs before that is muhaddith."
"5478","(5478) Hushaym told us, he said: A sheikh from Quraysh told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: I heard him narrating on the authority of Ibn Umar, He said: The call to prayer on Friday; That which occurs when the imam emerges, and that which occurs before that is muhaddith."
"5479","(5479) Shababhi told us, he said: Hisham bin Al-Ghaz told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: The first call to prayer is on Friday. Heresy"
"5480","(5480) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The first person to narrate the first call to prayer was Uthman, to call the people to prayer. Markets"
"5481","(5481) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he narrated to them: That the call to prayer was in the era of the Prophet May the peace and blessings of God be upon him when he left. Then, when he finished the sermon, the prayer was established. (Bukhari 912)"
"5482","(5482) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The call to prayer was when the Imam appeared, so Amir narrated The believers, Othman, the third call to prayer upon Al-Zawra’, so that the people may gather."
"5483","(5483) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin al-Ghaz told us, he said: I asked Nafi’ the client of Ibn Omar about the first call to prayer on the day. Friday? He said: Ibn Omar said: An heresy."
"5484","(5484) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Farwa, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. In the morning prayer, on the day of Friday, it is recited: (Al-Sajdah) and a surah from Al-Mufassal."
"5485","(5485) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was desirable for it to be recited on Friday. With a surah in which you prostrate."
"5486","(5486) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I have never witnessed Ibn Abbas reciting on a Friday prayer. Except for: (The Messenger of God was sent down), and (Has it come upon man)."
"5487","(5487) Yazeed bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I did not pray. He succeeded Ibn Abbas on Friday morning, unless he recited a surah in which he prostrated."
"5488","(5488) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Safiyya, on the authority of Ali; At dawn on the day of Friday, he recited Surah Al-Hashr and Surah Al-Jumu'ah."
"5489","(5489) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: They used to recite a surah in it on Friday prayers. He prostrated, so I asked Muhammad, and he said: I do not know of any harm in him."
"5490","(5490) Abdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday prayers: “Al-Ma’am Revelation” and “Has Al-Mutaz” There is a period of eternity upon man. (Tirmidhi 520, Abu Dawud 1067)"
"5491","(5491) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Ibrahim bin Abd believed us. Al-Rahman ibn Awf while we were in Medina, so I prayed the morning prayer behind him on Friday, and he recited: (The Mother of God was revealed) and {"
"5492","(5492) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu"
"5493","(5493) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Hamza al-A’war, on the authority of Ibrahim; He led them in prayer at dawn on Friday, so he recited with them: (کیعص)۔"
"5494","(5494) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Salem On the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the Eid and Friday prayers: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, And {Has the hadith of al-Ghashiya reached you?} And when the two vows come together on a day, it is recited between them. (Muslim 62. Abu Dawud 1115)"
"5495","(5495) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Rafi’, who said: He was appointed successor. Marwan led Abu Hurairah in Medina, and he went out to Mecca, so Abu Hurairah led us in prayer in congregation, and he recited a surah. The plural in the first prostration, and in the last prostration: {When the hypocrites come to you}"
"5496","(5496) Abdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in congregation the surahs of the congregation, and {When the hypocrites come to you}"
"5497","(5497) Ali told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Zayd ibn Uqba, on the authority of Samurah, he said: It was The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited in congregation: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Has the hadith of the cheater reached you}. (Abu Dawud 1188, An-Nasa’i 1739)"
"5498","(5498) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of people from the people of Medina. Abu Ja`far said: He used to recite in congregation the surahs of the congregation and the hypocrites. As for the surahs of the congregation, he would bring good tidings of them. The believers and incite them, and as for the Surah of the Hypocrites, He comforts the hypocrites with it and rebukes them with it."
"5499","(5499) Abdi and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id, who said: I prayed the congregational prayer behind Abu Musa. So he recited with: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and {Has the hadith of the cheater reached you}"
"5500","(5500) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, who said: I prayed behind Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and my father. Bakr bin Amr recited the Jumu’ah surah in the first rak’ah, and in the second rak’ah he recited the surah of the jumu’ah, and in the second rak’ah he recited: {Glorify the name of your Lord The highest}"
"5501","(5501) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning recitation on Friday, he said: The imam recites whatever he wants."
"5502","(5502) Hushaym bin Bashir and Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Awf bin Hasira. ; In the hour that is hoped for in congregation: between the time when the imam emerges and the prayer is finished."
"5503","(5503) Hushaym told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, he said: Between the afternoon and... That the sun sets."
"5504","(5504) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Abu Hurairah, who said: The hour that is mentioned in the Friday prayer: the period between the afternoon prayer until the sun sets."
"5505","(5505) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, the same."
"5506","(5506) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: I was with Ibn Umar, and he was asked about Al-Sa’i. Which is in the Friday prayer? He said: So I said: This is the hour that God chose for it, or during it is prayer. He said: Then he wiped my head and bestowed his blessings upon me. And he liked what I said."
"5507","(5507) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Burda, who said: This is when the Imam emerges."
"5508","(5508) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn Zayd ibn Mu’hab Abu narrated to us. Abd al-Rahman al-Amluki, on the authority of Abu Umamah, who said: I hope that the hour in the congregation will be one of these. Hours: When the muezzin or the imam gives the call to prayer on the pulpit, or when the iqamah is given."
"5509","(5509) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to say this at noon, at the time of prayer."
"5510","(5510) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is not clear that the sale is forbidden until He will analyze it."
"5511","(5511) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It is after the afternoon prayer."
"5512","(5512) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Sulayman bin Qurm told us, on the authority of Abu Habib, on the authority of Nubl, on the authority of Salama Bint Afi`a, she said: I was with Aisha with her wives, and I heard her say: The day of Jumu’ah is like the day of Arafah. And indeed, there is an Hour in which the doors of mercy will be opened. So we said: What Hour? She said: When the caller calls for prayer."
"5513","(5513) Ubaidah bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Sinan bin Habib, on the authority of Nubl bint Badr, on the authority of Salama bint Afi’a, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The day of Friday is like the day of Arafah, on which the doors of mercy are opened, and on it there is no one who seeks to ask. God does not give anything to a servant unless He gives it to him. It was said: What is his hour? She said: When the muezzin calls the morning prayer."
"5514","(5514) Ahmad bin Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The Hour that you hope for Friday after Asr."
"5515","(5515) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, and Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a sermon. When a man came and stepped on people's necks on the day of Friday, until he sat close to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when he had finished His prayers, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O so-and-so, did you not gather? He said: O Messenger of God, did you not see me? He said: I saw you being selfish and hurting me. (Abu Dawud 1111, Ibn Khuzaymah 1811)"
"5516","(5516) Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Musa bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, he said: Example The one who jumps around people's necks on the day of Friday prayer while the imam is delivering the sermon, is like one who lifts his feet into the fire and places them in the fire."
"5517","(5517) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid, he said: Othman bin Abdullah bin Mohab told me, he said: He said: Saeed bin Al-Musayyab: Because I pray the Friday prayer freely, it is more beloved to me than skipping it."
"5518","(5518) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hassan, he said: I saw Urwah bin Al-Mughirah came to the congregation, and when he finished, he stood up, i.e., and did not skip a beat."
"5519","(5519) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad said: They say: Muhammad jumps over the necks of people. On the day of Friday, I will not skip, but I will come and stand up, and the man will recognize me, and he will make room for me."
"5520","(5520) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid Al-Asam, on the authority of Abu Qais, who said: Abdullah bin Masoud entered the mosque. On the day of Friday, he was wearing beautiful white clothes. He saw a place where he ran and sat down and did not move further."
"5521","(5521) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in him stepping over people’s necks if he is in The mosque is spacious."
"5522","(5522) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Shurayh coming on the day of the Friday prayer and the imam. He was giving a sermon, but he sat down, that is, he did not skip a beat."
"5523","(5523) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Omar bin Atiyya, on the authority of Salman, who said: Beware of crossing the necks of people on Friday, and sit where the Friday prayer reaches you."
"5524","(5524) Waki’ and Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salih, the client of the twins, who said: I heard Abu Hurairah He says: Because I pray freely, I love it more than stepping over people’s necks on the day of Friday prayer."
"5525","(5525) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Juwayriyah ibn Asma`, on the authority of Khawat ibn Bukair, on the authority of Ka`b, who said: To let I love the gathering more than stepping over people’s necks."
"5526","(5526) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Some of the princes made their engagements long, so I became weary. Until I made her bloody, then I got up and took the whips, so I went and left."
"5527","(5527) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Siwar, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid ibn Sabrah; Salim told Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, he said: When the Emir came to us, the crowd came, and he gathered with us, and he still preached and recited. He wrote until the time for Friday prayer had passed, and he did not stop and pray. Al-Qasim said to him: Why did you get up and pray? He said: No, by God. I was afraid that he would be said: A man from the family of Omar. He said: Why did you pray sitting? He said: No. He said: What did you nod to? He said: No, he said: Then he continued delivering the sermon and reading until the afternoon time had passed and he did not stop and pray, so Al-Qasim said to him: So what? Did you stand up and pray? He said: No, he said: Why did you pray sitting? He said: No. He said: What did you nod to? He said: No."
"5528","(5528) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utbah Al-Zuhri said: Al-Hajjaj delayed the Friday prayer, so when he prayed, Abu Juhayfy prayed with him, then he got up and led it in prayer. Two rak'ahs, then he said: O Abu Bakr, I bear witness to you that it is the afternoon prayer."
"5529","(5529) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, who said: Al-Hajjaj used to delay Friday, so I was praying, and Ibrahim and Sa`id bin Jubayr were praying the noon prayer, then we would talk and he would give a sermon, then We pray with them, then we make it a voluntary prayer."
"5530","(5530) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim, who said: I was sitting with Masruq and Abu Ubaidah for a while. Ziyad, when the time for prayer began, they stood up and prayed, then they sat until the muezzin called the call to prayer and the imam came out, they stood up and prayed. With him, and they do it in the afternoon."
"5531","(5531) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hashim; Al-Hajjaj delayed the prayer, so Abu Wael nodded while he was sitting."
"5532","(5532) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of His father; Al-Walid bin Uqba delayed the prayer with the Kufa while I was sitting with my father in the mosque, so Abdullah stood up and performed the prayer. So he prayed for the people, then Al-Walid ibn Uqba sent to him: What made you do what you did? Has there come to you from the Commander of the Faithful a matter that happened before us, so he listened and obeyed, or did you innovate what you did today? He said: No matter has come to me from the Commander of the Faithful, and God forbid that I should be an innovator. Father of God and His Messenger, we should wait for you. With our prayers while you are in your needs."
"5533","(5533) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: I said to a brother: Al-Hajjaj dies in congregation. He said: He was discreet. Yes? He said: I said: Yes, he said: Pray in your house at its appointed time, and do not miss the congregational prayer."
"5534","(5534) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: Raising the hands on the day of congregational prayer is a hadith."
"5535","(5535) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The first to raise his hands in the crowd are the servants of God. Bin Abdullah bin Muammar."
"5536","(5536) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: He hated the supplications of those they called upon. On Friday, he did not raise his hands."
"5537","(5537) Ibn Numayr and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Murr, on the authority of Masruq, who said: The imam was raised On the day of Friday, his hand was on the pulpit, and the people raised their hands, and Masruq said: What’s wrong with them? May God cut it off. Their hands"
"5538","(5538) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amara bin Ruwaibiah; He saw Bishr bin Marwan raising his hands and calling, until he almost lay down behind him."
"5539","(5539) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amara ibn Ruwaibi, who said: Bishr ibn Marwan saw someone raising His hands on the pulpit, and he said: May God bless these hands. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. More than that, he said with his hand like this, and pointed with his finger, the rosary."
"5540","(5540) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-A’mash, who said: Abdullah’s companions used to pray with The chosen one is the plural, and they will be rewarded for it."
"5541","(5541) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Uqba al-Asadi, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Suleiman; That Abu Wael gathered with Al-Mukhtar."
"5542","(5542) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Salih bin Sa’id, who said: I went out with Omar bin Abdul Aziz to As-Suwayda’ appeared, and when the congregation arrived, the muezzin called the call to prayer, and they gathered pebbles for him. He said: So he stood up and delivered the sermon, then the congregation led the prayer. Two rak'ahs, then he said: The imam gathers wherever he is."
"5543","(5543) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Suwayd, he said: Mu’awiyah led us in prayer. The gathering with palm trees in the morning, then we delivered the sermon."
"5544","(5544) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad (h) and on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Abi Hariri, they said: Whoever does not pray in the mosque, there is no prayer for him."
"5545","(5545) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in praying on Friday prayers. The dam"
"5546","(5546) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in praying on the day of Friday prayers. Al-Rahba, and if he is able to enter, then there is no prayer for him."
"5547","(5547) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, he said: I saw Urwah bin Al-Mughiriya bin Shu’bah praying in The dam"
"5548","(5548) Muhammad bin Bishr and Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa; That Abu Hurairah came to some men sitting in the spacious hall, and said: Enter the mosque, for there is no Friday prayer except in the mosque."
"5549","(5549) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he said: There is no Friday prayer for the one who prays in Al-Rahba, unless he is unable to enter."
"5550","(5550) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Salat Al-Ruba’i, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I heard him say: If you do not hear the imam’s recitation on Friday, then read."
"5551","(5551) Hatim narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The master of days is Friday. (Ibn Khuzaymah 1728, Bayhaqi 2971)"
"5552","(5552) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Hubira, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Indeed, the Lord of the Days is Friday, and the master of the month is Ramadan."
"5553","(5553) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Abu Burda bin Abi Musa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Indeed, in the Friday prayer there is an hour, in which God does not supplicate to a Muslim servant for anything but he responds. (Bukhari 64000 Muslim 584)"
"5554","(5554) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Abu al-Ash’ath al-San’ani, on the authority of Aws Ibn Aws said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: One of the best of your days is the day of Friday, on which Adam was created. And in it is the blow, and in it is the thunderbolt. (Abu Dawud 1526. Ahmad 4/8)"
"5555","(5555) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: No. The sun will rise on a day that is greater than Friday. When it rises, everything panics for it except the two heavy ones, which Reckoning and punishment are upon them."
"5556","(5556) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Damra, on the authority of Ka’b, who said: Charity is multiplied. Friday"
"5557","(5557) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Ka’b; On the Day of Friday, the creatures, the jinn and mankind will be terrified, and the good and the bad will be multiplied on it, and the For the Day of Resurrection."
"5558","(5558) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Kathir bin Abdullah Al-Muzani narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: Friday is an hour of the day, during which the servant does not ask for anything except He was given his question. It was said: What kind of hour is he? He said: Where the prayer is performed until the end of it. (Tirmidhi 490, Ibn Majah 1138)"
"5559","(5559) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Zuhair bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Lubab bin Abdul-Mundhir, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The day Friday is the master of days, the greatest of them in the sight of God, and greater in the sight of God than the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Fitr, in which there are five times: God created Adam in him, and God brought down Adam in him, and in him God took Adam to death, and in him he did not ask the servant of God. There is nothing in it unless He gives it to him, as long as he does not ask for something forbidden, and in it the Hour will come. There is no close angel, nor land, nor There are no skies, no winds, no mountains, no sea except that they will twilight from the Day of Judgment. (Ibn Majah 1084. Ahmad 3/430)"
"5560","(5560) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings be upon him: Gabriel came to me, and in his hand was like a white mirror, and in it was like a black spot, so I said: Gabriel! What is this? He said: This is Friday.\n He said: I said: What is the Friday prayer? He said: There is something better for you in it. He said: I said: What do we have in it? He said: It will be a feast for you and your people after you, and the Jews and Christians will follow you. He said: I said: What do we have in it? He said: There is an hour for you in it. A Muslim servant does not agree with it. He asks God for something from this world and the hereafter. He He has an oath unless he gives it to him, or he has no oath unless something better than him is stored up for him, or he seeks refuge Of evil, and it is decreed upon him. Unless he averts from him some affliction that is greater than it.\n He said: I said to him: What is this joke about it? He said: It is the Hour, and it will rise on Friday, and with us it is the master of days, and we will call on it on the Day of Resurrection. The Day of More\n He said: I said: What is that? He said: Because your Lord, Blessed and Most High, took in Paradise a valley of white musk, so when it was the day of Friday, He would descend. Of the two upper chambers upon His throne, Blessed and Most High, then He surrounded the throne with platforms of gold crowned with jewels, then The prophets will come and sit on it, and the people of the rooms will come down and sit on that hill, then Their Lord, Blessed and Most High, appears to them, then He says: Ask Me and I will give it to you. He said: Then they will ask of Him satisfaction, and He says: My satisfaction, I will grant you My abode and grant you My honor, so ask of Me and I will give it to you. He said: So they will ask of Me for My satisfaction. He said: And He will testify to them that He is pleased with them. He said: Then it will be opened for them what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and no thought has occurred to me. Human heart, he said: This is the extent of your departure from the day of Friday.\n He said: Then he will rise, and the prophets, the truthful ones, and the martyrs will rise with him, and the people of the rooms will return to their rooms, and there will be a circle. It is white, there is no cleft, no cleft, no red pearl, or green aquamarine. It has rooms and doors. It is rain-fed, and therein are its rivers and its fruits hanging down. He said: They are not in need of anything greater than them until the Day of Judgment. assembly, that they may increase their sight of their Lord, and that they may increase in honor from Him. (Tabarani 6713, Bazzar 3519)"
"5561","(5561) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings be upon him: Gabriel came to me with a white mirror with a black spot on it. He said: So I said: What is this? He said: This is Friday and in it is the Hour. (Abu Yali 4089)"
"5562","(5562) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Al-Aghar, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, On the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: He who hastens to the gathering is like one who guides his body, then like one who is guided by a cow. Then like the Mahdi a sheep, then like the Mahdi a bird. (Bukhari 929. Muslim 24)"
"5563","(5563) His youth narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Maqbari, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin And on the authority of Salman Al-Khair, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: A man should not wash himself on the day of Friday prayer and purify himself. He purified himself as much as he could, cleansed himself of oil, or touched perfume from his house, then he departed, making no distinction between them. Two, then pray what God has decreed for him, then listen when the imam speaks, unless he will be forgiven for what happened between him and the crowd. The Hereafter (Bukhari 883. Ahmad 5/440)"
"5564","(5564) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ali bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Aws bin Khaled, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The angels are at the gates of the mosque recording the people. To their homes: So-and-so came on such-and-such an hour, so-and-so came on such-and-such an hour, so-and-so came and the imam was delivering a sermon, he came So-and-so performed the prayer but did not realize the sermon. (Ahmad 2/343, Tayalisi 2565)"
"5565","(5565) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I was informed that the rain was intense on the day of the Friday prayer, but he did not gather."
"5566","(5566) Yahya bin Sa’id al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Kathir, a client of Ibn Samurah, who said: I passed by Abd al-Rahman bin Samarra, and he was sitting at my door. He said: What is wrong with your prince? I said: Didn't you collect? He said: This barrenness prevented us from it."
"5567","(5567) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith; Ibn Abbas ordered his caller, so he called out on a rainy day on Friday: Prayer while traveling, prayer while traveling."
"5568","(5568) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’; A son of Sa`id bin Zaid bin Nufayl was on land of his own in Al-Aqiq, at the head of a few miles from Medina, so Ibn Umar came On the morning of Friday, he mentioned his complaint to him, so he went to him and left the Friday prayer."
"5569","(5569) Abdul-Wahhab told us, he said: I asked Yunus about a man whose mother, or father, or relative, is dying. Is there an excuse for not performing congregational prayers? He said: Al-Hassan used to make a concession in it to the person attending the funeral, and he was afraid for her, or the man was afraid."
"5570","(5570) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If your son is shouted at on the day of the Friday prayer and the imam is giving the sermon, So rise to it, and leave the group."
"5571","(5571) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: A man said to Abu Majliz: Or did I say to him: I will come to the congregation and I will Does my stomach complain? He said: inability."
"5572","(5572) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, and the like."
"5573","(5573) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abul-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is not upon the fearful, nor upon the servant. The one who serves his family, nor the funeral guardian, nor the blind man if he does not find a leader."
"5574","(5574) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, who said: I heard Al-Hasan and he was asked about Al-Khaif. What is the burden on him? He said: What is his fear? He said: From the Sultan. He said: Indeed, he has an excuse."
"5575","(5575) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is obligatory for a blind man to join prayers if he finds a leader, and for If the slave pays the tax. He said: He used to give permission to the fearful in congregation."
"5576","(5576) Zaid bin Harun, Muhammad bin Bishr, and Ibn Idris narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Amr informed us, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Sufyan al-Hadrami said: I heard Abu al-Ja`d al-Dhamri, who had companions, say: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Whoever abandons the congregation three times out of negligence, his heart will be sealed. (Tirmidhi 5000, Abu Dawud 1045)"
"5577","(5577) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawwi informed us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abi Salam, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Mina, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Ibn Abbas; They bore witness against the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said, while he was on the pillars of the pulpit: Let them stop. Some people will abandon the Friday prayers, or God will seal their hearts, and they will be recorded as among the heedless. (Muslim 400, An-Nasa’i 1658)"
"5578","(5578) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hammam bin Yahya informed us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Qadamah bin Wabarah. Al-Ujaifi, on the authority of Samurah ibn Jundub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever abandons the congregation without an excuse Let him give a dinar in charity, and if he does not find it, then half a dinar. (Abu Dawud 1046. Ibn Hibban 2788)"
"5579","(5579) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Al-Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whoever abandons the congregation Three times in a row, God set a seal on his heart."
"5580","(5580) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-Abbas bin Abdullah bin Ma’abad, he said: He said: Abu Hurairah : I do not like to have reddish blessings, nor to miss out on Friday prayers except with an excuse."
"5581","(5581) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja’far, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Perhaps one of you will take a young boy from the sheep at the head of two miles, or three, and it will be combined. Then he does not bear witness to her, then she is but he does not bear witness to her, then she is but he does not bear witness to her, then God seals his heart. (Ahmad 3/332, Abu Ali 2198)"
"5582","(5582) Al-Fudayl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he heard it from him, on the authority of Abdullah, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a people who were staying behind from the congregation: I wished to order a man to pray. With the people, then their houses were burned for the men who stayed behind from the crowd."
"5583","(5583) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man went to Ibn Abbas for a month, asking him about a man. He prays in prayer all night and fasts during the day, and he does not witness the prayer in congregation or in congregation. He said: In Hell."
"5584","(5584) Hushaym told us, saying: Yazid bin Abi Ziyad informed us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Aazib said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is a right for Muslims for one of them to bathe. On the day of Friday, he should touch some perfume if he has it, but if he does not have perfume, then water is perfume for him."
"5585","(5585) Abdi told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Uthman bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: It is a Muslim’s right, if it is Friday, to use the siwak, to wear appropriate clothing, and to use perfume. It's good if it is."
"5586","(5586) Abu Asama told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Whenever Ibn Umar went to the congregation, he would take a bath. And he perfumed himself with the best perfume he had."
"5587","(5587) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I say according to my opinion, and he touches perfume if He was there"
"5588","(5588) Muhammad bin Bishr and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Utbah, on the authority of Ibn Mughaffal said: She should be washed and perfumed, if necessary."
"5589","(5589) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Wear your best clothes on the day of Friday prayer, and wear perfume. The best you can find."
"5590","(5590) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shaddad Abi Talha, on the authority of Mu’awiyah ibn Qurayh, he said: I reached thirty of Muzainah. All of them have been stabbed, stabbed, struck, or struck. When it is the day of Friday, they should wash themselves and wear better clothing. Their clothes, and they perfumed themselves, then they went and prayed two rak’ahs, then they sat down, and spread knowledge."
"5591","(5591) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Omar used to embroider his clothes in every Friday prayer."
"5592","(5592) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to wear his red cloak on the day of Friday prayers, and he would go dark on the day of the Eids. (Ibn Saad 451)"
"5593","(5593) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to perform ablution for the congregation. Such as taking a bath from ritual impurity, putting on one of his best clothes, then going out until he comes to the place of prayer."
"5594","(5594) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: I realized The Companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the Companions of Badr and the Companions of Shajara, when it is the day of Friday, they dress better. Then, if they had any perfume, they would touch it with it, then they would go to the Friday prayer meeting."
"5595","(5595) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: Consider The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed the people on the day of Friday, thus preparing them, and said: It would not harm a man if he took Two garments for this day? (Ibn Majah 1095; Ibn Khuzaymah 1765)"
"5596","(5596) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, the same, and he added to it: two garments in which he will wear."
"5597","(5597) Marhum bin Abdul Aziz told us that he heard Thabit Al-Bunani say: I was with Anas bin Malik on the day He gathered them together, and when he heard the call to prayer, he said: Get up and we will go."
"5598","(5598) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: {So strive to the remembrance of Allah} He said: With his heart."
"5599","(5599) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Striving is action."
"5600","(5600) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Masruq; {So strive to the remembrance of God} He said: The time."
"5601","(5601) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Dinar, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, who said: His exhortation Imam"
"5602","(5602) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b, who said: Striving is action."
"5603","(5603) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Rashid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In his saying: (So strive to the remembrance of Allah) He said: By Allah, it is not by running on foot, and they intended to perform the prayer Except that peace and dignity be upon them, but with hearts, intentions, and humility. (Bukhari 6350, Muslim 155)"
"5604","(5604) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah used to recite it: (So go to The remembrance of God) and He says: If I had recited it: (So strive), I would have striven until my cloak falls."
"5605","(5605) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Kharsha, he said: It was recited by Umar ibn al-Khattab: {So go to Remembrance of Allah}"
"5606","(5606) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, in his saying: {Then when the prayer is completed, disperse throughout the land. And seek of the bounty of God."
"5607","(5607) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Mujahid; (Then when the prayer is completed, disperse throughout the land.) They said: If he wants, he can do it, and if he wants, he does not do it."
"5608","(5608) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Bara’, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed them on the day of Eid, and in his hand was a bow or a staff. (Abdul Razzaq 5658 and Ahmed 282)"
"5609","(5609) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, who said: I saw Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz giving a sermon with his hands in his hands. rod"
"5610","(5610) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il; Ka'b saw a jar with a staff in his hand, so he said: This is only suitable for a shepherd or a governor."
"5611","(5611) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, who said: I heard his followers say about a man who opened the prayer with the imam on the day of Friday prayer, but he did not He could neither bow nor prostrate until the imam had prayed. He said: Al-Hasan and Ibrahim used to say: He should pray two rak’ahs. It means Friday."
"5612","(5612) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, who said: He was asked about a man who performed two rak’ahs on the day of Friday prayer, but he was not able to perform it. Prostration until the imam says the salaam?"
"5613","(5613) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: A man said to Nafi’: I was crowded on the day of Friday, so I was not able to bow. And prostration, and he said: As for me, if I were, I would nod."
"5614","(5614) Muhammad bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If people crowd together in the congregation and you are not able To prostrate, then wait until when they stand up, prostrate."
"5615","(5615) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man cleanses his nails in every... All together"
"5616","(5616) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Ibn Hamid bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father; He said regarding someone who trims his nails on the day of Friday: God has removed the disease from them and brought healing into them."
"5617","(5617) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim bin Yassar, on the authority of his father; He used to pray with the two pens on Friday, meaning the short ones."
"5618","(5618) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, he said: Mandal narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Abi Ata’, he said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafiyyah. He cleanses his nails on Friday."
"5619","(5619) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Al-Haytham, who said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr being purified. His nails in prayer."
"5620","(5620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: There is no harm in drinking while the imam is delivering the sermon."
"5621","(5621) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Asmaa, who said: Whoever recites: {Say: “Allah is One” And the two Mu’awwidhatayn on the day of Friday prayer seven times in their sitting, it is preserved for the like of them."
"5622","(5622) Affan told us, he said: Abdul Wahid told us, he said: Yunus told us, he said: Al-Hasan used to count the poor on the day The congregation while the imam is delivering the sermon. He says to them: Sit down. He said: Ikrimah did not see them all together."
"5623","(5623) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Sinan bin Habib, he said: I said to Ibrahim: Have you missed the Friday prayer? He said: More prostration."
"5624","(5624) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Concerning the people of the prisons, he said: They gathered for prayer on Friday."
"5625","(5625) A sheikh of ours narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The people of the prisons do not have to do the same."
"5626","(5626) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Yazid bin Ibrahim narrated to us; Al-Hasan was asked about a man who broke his fast on Friday, so he went to perform ablution, and he came while the imam had prayed? He said: He prays four times."
"5627","(5627) Waki’ told us, he said: I asked Sufyan about a man who opened the Friday prayer with the imam, so he went to perform ablution. So he came while the imam had prayed? He said: He prays two rak'ahs as long as he does not speak."
"5628","(5628) Hushaym bin Bashir narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Hafs bin Ubad Allah bin Anas, on the authority of Anas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to break his fast on the Day of Fitr with dates, then go out in the morning. (Tirmidhi 543. Ibn Majah 1754)"
"5629","(5629) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Feed on the Day of Fitr before He went out to the prayer hall."
"5630","(5630) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is part of the Sunnah to go out. Break the fast before the prayer, and do not leave until you have eaten. (Tabarani 11296. Bazzar 651)"
"5631","(5631) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, he said: I went out in the morning with Muawiyah bin Suwayd bin Muqrin on the day of Fitr."
"5632","(5632) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibn Maqil; He licked a lick of honey, then came out."
"5633","(5633) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, who said: Feed the food on the Day of Fitr before you go out."
"5634","(5634) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, who said: I came to Safwan bin Mahrez on the day of Fitr. So I sat at his door until he came out to me, and he said to me like an apologist: On this day he was ordered to attack a man. Of his food before dawn, and I missed something, that is what imprisoned me, and as for the other, it delayed his food. Until he comes back."
"5635","(5635) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Ibn Sirin used to bring a sample of bread during the Eids. He used to eat some of it before morning. He said: Ibn Aoun says that he refrains from urinating."
"5636","(5636) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad; He passed by a grocer on the day of Eid, and he took some of it and ate it."
"5637","(5637) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is part of the Sunnah to eat food on the Day of Fitr before To go out in the morning and delay eating on the Day of Sacrifice until you return."
"5638","(5638) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul-Rahman, who said: Al-Aswad used to order us to eat food before morning on the day of breaking the fast."
"5639","(5639) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Masra bin Ma’abad, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Abla, on the authority of Umm al-Darda’, she said: Before the morning of the day of breaking the fast, even if it is a date."
"5640","(5640) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Sa’ib bin Zayd, he said: The Sunnah has passed for you to eat before dawn on the day of breaking the fast."
"5641","(5641) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : If you go out on the day of Eid, meaning breaking the fast, eat even if it is a date."
"5642","(5642) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Abdullah bin Rahimah, who said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz On the Day of Breakfast, he gave a sermon and said: This is a day on which some food and some drink were sought, so some food And some drink."
"5643","(5643) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said: Feed on the Day of Fitr. Before you go out."
"5644","(5644) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It has reached him that Tamim bin Salamah went out on the Day of Fitr. And a friend of his was with him, and he said to his friend: Have you eaten anything? He said: No, so Tamim walked to a grocer and asked him if he would give him some dates, or something else, so he did, and his friend gave them to him. So he ate it. So Abraham said: Walking to a man to ask him is more difficult for him than forsaking food if he were to abandon it."
"5645","(5645) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Were you afflicted with something before you went out in the morning?"
"5646","(5646) His youth narrated to us, he said: His people narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of a man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. ; He used to order people to eat on the day of Iftar before coming to the place of prayer."
"5647","(5647) Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Malik informed me, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: They were They are ordered to eat before the morning of the day of breaking the fast."
"5648","(5648) Ahmad bin Abdul-Malik bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, On the authority of Ata’ bin Yassar, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to eat every day. Breaking the fast before going out to the prayer place. (Ahmad 3/28, Abd al-Razzaq 5735)"
"5649","(5649) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Ubaid Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to go out to the place of prayer on the day of Eid, and not eat anything."
"5650","(5650) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: If he tastes, it is good, and if he does not taste, then no. Unfortunately"
"5651","(5651) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to us: Who among you is able to He comes to the Eid walking, so let him do it."
"5652","(5652) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is Sunnah to come to the Eid walking. (Tirmidhi 530, Ibn Majah 1296)"
"5653","(5653) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, who said: Omar ibn al-Khattab went out on the day of the breaking of the fast, or On the day of Adha, he went out in a cotton dress, wearing it, walking."
"5654","(5654) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim; He disliked riding to the Eids and Friday prayers."
"5655","(5655) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Hafsiya, who said: I saw Al-Hasan coming to the Eid riding."
"5656","(5656) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar used to pray the morning prayer in the mosque of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, then he goes in the morning as he is to the prayer place."
"5657","(5657) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala; He used to leave with Saeed bin Al-Musayyab in the morning, when the imam said the salaam on the day of Eid, until he came to the place of prayer. At the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt, he sits at the two gates."
"5658","(5658) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I prayed the dawn prayer in this mosque on the day of Fitr. Then, when Abu Abdul Rahman and Abdullah bin Maqil finished the prayer, they left, and I went out with them to the graveyard."
"5659","(5659) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ubaid al-Mukhtab, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to pray Fajr and they have their clothes on, meaning the day of Eid."
"5660","(5660) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Let your morning journey on the Day of Fitr be from your mosque to Your prayers"
"5661","(5661) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: Urwa would not come until the Eid. The sun rises."
"5662","(5662) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali, Amir, and Ata’, they said: Do not go out on that day. Eid until the sun rises."
"5663","(5663) Shababi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Issa bin Sahl bin Rafi’ bin Khadij; He saw his grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij and his sons sitting in the mosque until, when the sun rose, they prayed two rak’ahs, then They go to the prayer place, and that is for breaking the fast and for the sacrifice."
"5664","(5664) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I went to Abraham on the day of Eid, and found him having prayed and upon him. Her clothes"
"5665","(5665) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; In the morning on the day of Eid, he used to say “Allahu Akbar” and raise his voice until he reached the imam."
"5666","(5666) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdullah bin Abi Qatada, he said: I see it on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim; That Abu Qatada used to say “Allahu Akbar” on the day of Eid and remember Allah."
"5667","(5667) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, would go out on the Day of Fitr and say “Allahu Akbar” until he came to the place of prayer, and until He completes the prayer, so when he completes the prayer, he stops reciting the takbeer. (Daraqutni 6. Bayhaqi 279)"
"5668","(5668) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I went out with Abu Abdul Rahman and Ibn Maqil, and Abu Abd al-Rahman used to say “Allahu Akbar”, raising his voice with “Allahu Akbar”, and Ibn Maqil used to say: There is no god but Allah alone, without any partner. To Him belongs, to Him belongs the dominion and to Him is praise, and He has power over all things."
"5669","(5669) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I went out with Sa’id bin Jubayr. And Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, and they continued to say “Allahu Akbar” and they commanded everyone they passed by to say “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5670","(5670) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I used to go out with our companions; Ibrahim, Khaythama, and Abu Salih on the day of Eid, so do not say “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5671","(5671) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: A Muslim man narrated to me, on the authority of Hanash Abi The pilgrim; On the day of Adha, Ali said the takbir until the end of the Eid."
"5672","(5672) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is part of the Sunnah to say “Allahu Akbar” on the day of Eid."
"5673","(5673) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, he said: I said to Al-Hakam and Hammad: Should I say Akbar when I go out to the Eid? They said: Yes."
"5674","(5674) Hafs bin Ghayath and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa; That his father used to say “Allahu Akbar” on the day of Eid."
"5675","(5675) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: People used to say “Allahu Akbar” in Eid, when they leave their homes until they come to the prayer place, and until the imam comes out, so when the imam comes out they keep silent, So when he says “Allahu Akbar,” they say “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5676","(5676) Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I was leading Ibn Abbas on the day of Eid, and he heard People say “Allahu Akbar”, so he said: What is the matter with the people? I said: They say “Allahu Akbar”, he said: “They say Allahu Akbar”? He said: Does the imam say “Allahu Akbar”? I said: No. He said: Are people crazy?"
"5677","(5677) Husayn bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zaydah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Ali (h) and on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Abi Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” after the Fajr prayer on the day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the last days of Tashreeq, and he would say “Allahu Akbar” after The afternoon"
"5678","(5678) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of Umair bin Saeed, on the authority of Ali; He used to say takbeer from the dawn prayer on the day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."
"5679","(5679) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Abdullah used to say “Allahu Akbar” during the Fajr prayer. On the Day of Arafah he leads to the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice, saying: Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, There is no god but Allah, God is great, God is great, praise be to God."
"5680","(5680) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ghaylan ibn Jami’, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to say takbeer from the dawn prayer on the day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the day of Sacrifice."
"5681","(5681) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Awan, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Omar; He used to say takbeer from the morning prayer on the day of Arafah until the noon prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."
"5682","(5682) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Abdul Hamid bin Abi Rabah Al-Shami, on the authority of a man From the people of the Levant, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the last days of Tashreeq, saying “Allahu Akbar” in the afternoon prayer."
"5683","(5683) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Abi Rabah, he said: A man from the family of Al-Sham, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit: He used to say takbeer from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the afternoon prayer on the last days of Tashreeq."
"5684","(5684) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz used to pronounce the Eid takbeer from Dhuhr prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the last days of Tashreeq."
"5685","(5685) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say takbeer from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the afternoon prayer on the last days of Tashreeq."
"5686","(5686) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to say takbeer from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the afternoon prayer on the Day of Departure, meaning the first."
"5687","(5687) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: He says takbir after the prayer. Dhuhr is the Day of Sacrifice until the last days of Tashreeq."
"5688","(5688) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Tariq told us; He memorized the takbeer from Qays ibn Abi Hazim on the days of Tashreeq until he prayed the afternoon prayer, and he said takbeer afterwards."
"5689","(5689) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim; That Abu Wa’il used to say “Allahu Akbar” from the day of Arafah, from the morning prayer to the noon prayer, meaning from the Day of Sacrifice."
"5690","(5690) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” during the days of Tashreeq, from the noon prayer on the day of Arafat until the dawn prayer on the last days of Al-Tashreeq"
"5691","(5691) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Salama bin Nabit, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He used to say takbeer from the dawn prayer on the day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the last day of Tashreeq."
"5692","(5692) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Abu Bakkar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” from the Fajr prayer on the day of Arafah until the last days of Tashreeq, and he would not say “Allahu Akbar” in Maghrib: God. God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, praise be to God."
"5693","(5693) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say “Allahu Akbar” from the noon prayer on the day of Arafat until the noon prayer at the end of the day. The days of the East."
"5694","(5694) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Humaid; Al-Hasan used to say “Allahu Akbar” from the noon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice until the noon prayer of the first group."
"5695","(5695) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim. Others said: On the authority of Zayd bin Aws, on the authority of Alqamiya; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” on the day of Arafah, from the dawn prayer until the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice."
"5696","(5696) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to say “Allahu Akbar” on the Day of Arafah, and one of them was facing. The direction towards the direction of prayer: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest. Allah is the greatest, and praise be to Allah."
"5697","(5697) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” during the days of Tashreeq: “God is great, God is great, there is no god but God, and God is great, God is great.” Praise be to God."
"5698","(5698) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to say takbeer from the dawn prayer on the day of Arafah until the afternoon prayer on the Day of Sacrifice, so he mentioned an example of a hadith Wakee'"
"5699","(5699) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, saying: I said to Abu Ishaq: How was the takbeer of Ali? And Abdullah? He said: They used to say: Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is the greatest, Allah is the greatest, and praise be to Allah."
"5700","(5700) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Humayd informed us; Al-Hassan used to say “Allahu Akbar,” “Allahu Akbar,” three times."
"5701","(5701) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abu Bakkar, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that he used to say: God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, God is great, praise be to God."
"5702","(5702) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Jabir bin Samra, who said: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The two Eids are not repeated, nor twice, without the call to prayer, or the iqamah. (Muslim 604. Abu Dawud 1141)"
"5703","(5703) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He prayed the two Eids without the call to prayer or the iqamah. (Bukhari 960, Muslim 5)"
"5704","(5704) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on the day of Eid without the call to prayer or iqamah."
"5705","(5705) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer on the day of Eid at the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt, so he prayed before the sermon. He did not mention the call to prayer or the iqamah. (Bukhari 863. Ahmad 1/368)"
"5706","(5706) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Simak, who said: I saw Al-Mughirah bin Shu’abi and Al-Dahhak. Moreover, they pray on the Day of Fitr and on the Day of Eid al-Adha without the call to prayer or the iqamah."
"5707","(5707) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bah; He prayed on the day of Eid without the call to prayer or the iqamah."
"5708","(5708) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He used to say: There is no adhan or iqamah on the two Eids."
"5709","(5709) Khaled bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: There is no adhan or iqamah in it."
"5710","(5710) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; Ibn al-Zubayr asked Ibn Abbas? He said: And what came between them was good, so he said: Do not call the call to prayer, and do not perform the iqama. So when what came between them went wrong, he called the call to prayer and did not perform the iqama."
"5711","(5711) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The call to prayer for Eid is innovated."
"5712","(5712) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The first to introduce the call to prayer for Eid Muawiyah"
"5713","(5713) Salam Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no adhan, no iqamah for the two Eids, and no Recitation behind the imam."
"5714","(5714) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mughirah, who said: I said to Abu Wael: They were giving the call to prayer in Eid al-Adha and Eid al-Fitr? He said: No."
"5715","(5715) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, and Al-Hakam, who said: The call to prayer is on the day of Al-Adha and Al-Fitr. Heresy"
"5716","(5716) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: The first person to give the call to prayer for Eid was Ziyad."
"5717","(5717) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Zechariah informed us, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed on the day of Eid without the call to prayer or iqamah."
"5718","(5718) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Ali; He prayed on the day of Eid without the call to prayer or iqamah."
"5719","(5719) Ibn Uyaynah told us, he said: Ayoub told us, he said: I heard Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: I bear witness to The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed before the sermon, and then he delivered the sermon. (Bukhari 1449. Abu Dawud 1137)"
"5720","(5720) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I witnessed the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The day of Eid began with prayer before the sermon."
"5721","(5721) Abd Allah bin Sulaiman and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, and Omar used to pray the Eid prayers before the sermons. (Bukhari 957, Tirmidhi 531)"
"5722","(5722) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, led them in prayer on the day of Eid at the house of Kathir ibn al-Salt, so he led them in prayer before The engagement"
"5723","(5723) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressed us. He said the salaam on the Day of Sacrifice after the prayer. (Bukhari 955, Tirmidhi 1508)"
"5724","(5724) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Shu’abi informed us, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Qays, he said: I heard Jundub ibn Abd God says: I prayed with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Sacrifice, then he delivered a sermon. (Bukhari 9851, Muslim 1552)"
"5725","(5725) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Muslim, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I witnessed the Eid with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and with Abu Bakr and Omar, so they began to pray before the sermon. (Bukhari 962 and Muslim 602)"
"5726","(5726) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, a client of Ibn Azhar, who said: I witnessed the Eid with Omar ibn Al-Khattab started praying before the sermon. He said: Then I witnessed the Eid with Othman, so he started praying before the sermon. He said: I witnessed it with Ali, so he started praying before the sermon."
"5727","(5727) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Misra Abu Jamilah, who said: I witnessed the Eid with Ali, so when He prayed and delivered a sermon. He said: Othman used to do it."
"5728","(5728) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; Ibn al-Zubayr asked Ibn Abbas, saying: What should I do on this day, the day of Eid? And what came between them was good, so he said: Do not give the call to prayer, do not perform the qimam, and pray before the sermon. When the conversation between them took place, he called the call to prayer, performed the iqama, and delivered the sermon before the prayer."
"5729","(5729) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The prayer was during the two Eids before The engagement"
"5730","(5730) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Imam used to begin the day of Eid. He prays, then mounts his camel and addresses the women as often as he returns."
"5731","(5731) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Karim, who said: I heard Abu Al-Bakhtari on the day of Eid, and he heard a man He said: The prayer before the sermon, and he said: The Sunnah and the Lord of the Kaaba."
"5732","(5732) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Abu Hamza, the client of Yazid ibn al-Muhallab; Matar bin Najiya asked Saeed bin Jubayr about prayer on the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Fitr? So he ordered him to pray before the sermon, but the people disapproved of that, so Sa`id said: By God, it is well known. And God is known."
"5733","(5733) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Ali led the Eid with us, then He proposed to his wife."
"5734","(5734) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam, who said: It was People would begin with prayer, then continue with sermons, until, when the age came and the number of people in his time came, then it was He went to deliver a sermon, and the people turned away. When Omar saw that, he began the sermon until he concluded with prayer."
"5735","(5735) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’i, on the authority of his father, who said: Marwan brought out the pulpit, He began his sermon before the prayer, and a man stood up to him and said: O Marwan, you have violated the Sunnah. You took out the pulpit and did not He was leaving, and I started giving the sermon before the prayer, so Abu Sa`id said: Who is this? They said: So-and-so, and he said: This man has fulfilled his debt. (Muslim 79. Abu Dawud 1133)"
"5736","(5736) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, who said: The first to start With the sermon on the day of Eid before the prayer Marwan, then a man stood up to him and said: The prayer is before the sermon, so he said: He left what There you are. Abu Sa`id said: As for this man, he has fulfilled his obligation. (Muslim 78. Abu Dawud 1133)"
"5737","(5737) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated speaking while the imam was giving the sermon on the Day of the two Eids."
"5738","(5738) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He hated it"
"5739","(5739) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Awan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hated it"
"5740","(5740) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I went out with him on the day of Eid. When the imam delivered the sermon, he remained silent."
"5741","(5741) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I told him: He dislikes speaking about the Eid and the imam. Get engaged? He said: Yes."
"5742","(5742) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: Al-Hakam bin Utaiba spoke to me on the day of Eid while the imam was giving the sermon."
"5743","(5743) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman bin Ya`la al-Taifi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Abiyya, on the authority of his grandfather; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said the “Allahu Akbar” on Eid twelve days, seven on the first day, and five on the first day. The Hereafter (Abu Dawud 1144, Ahmad 2/180)"
"5744","(5744) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: He narrated to me. Abu Aisha, who was a companion of Abu Hurairah, said: I witnessed Saeed bin Al-Aas and he called Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari and he was removed. So he asked them about the takbir during the two Eids? Abu Musa said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say “Allahu Akbar” four times during the two Eids, just as he would pronounce “Allahu Akbar” on The funeral, he said: And Hudhayfy confirmed him, he said: Abu Musa said: And thus I used to lead the people of Basra in prayer while I was there. Abu Aisha said: I was present at that, so I never forgot his saying four things, like the takbeer at a funeral. (Abu Dawud 1146. Al-Bayhaqi 290)"
"5745","(5745) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Inform me of the witness of Sa’id ibn al-Aas. He was sent to me. He brought together four people from the people of the tree, and he asked them about saying “Allahu Akbar” during Eid? They said: Eight takbeers. He said: So I mentioned that to Ibn Sirin, and he said: He spoke the truth, but he neglected to say takbeers, so go ahead. Prayer"
"5746","(5746) Hushaym told us, he said: Mujalid told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: Abdullah used to teach us The takbeer in the two Eids is nine takbeers; Five in the first, four in the last, and he continues between the two qira’at."
"5747","(5747) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhall, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” nine times during Eid-ul-Fitr and Eid-ul-Adha; Five in the first, four in the last, and he continues between the two recitations."
"5748","(5748) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Musa (h) and on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; One of the princes of Kufa, Sufyan said: one of them was Sa`id ibn al-Aas, and he said: the other was al-Walid ibn Uqba, was sent to Abdullah bin Masoud, Hudhafi bin Al-Yaman, and Abdullah bin Qais, and he said: This Eid has come, so what do you see? So they entrusted their matter to Abdullah, and he said: Say “Allahu Akbar” nine times. “Allahu Akbar” with which you begin the prayer, then you say “Allahu Akbar” three times, then you recite a surah, then you pronounce “Allahu Akbar,” then you kneel, then you get up and recite Surah, then say “Allahu Akbar” four times, bowing with one of them."
"5749","(5749) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” when breaking his fast, eleven times; Six in the first rak'ah, and five in the last, starting with the recitation in the two rak'ahs, and five in the sacrifice; Three in the first rak'ah, and two in the last, starting with the recitation in the two rak'ahs."
"5750","(5750) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, and Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” thirteen times."
"5751","(5751) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; That Ibn Abbas said the takbir on the thirteenth of Eid; Seven in the first, and six in the last."
"5752","(5752) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He used to say “Allahu Akbar” in The first is seven takbeers, and the second is five, all of them before the recitation."
"5753","(5753) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” during the Eid, seven times in the first, with the opening takbeer, and in the last six. With the takbeer of the rak’ah, all of them are before the recitation."
"5754","(5754) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Kurdous, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: On the night of the Eid, he sent Al-Walid bin Uqba went to Ibn Masoud, Abu Masoud, Hudhayf, and Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari, and he said to them: The Eid Tomorrow, how do you say “Allahu Akbar”? Then Abdullah said: Get up and say “Allahu Akbar” four times, and recite the Opening of the Book and a surah from Al-Mufassal, not from its length. Nor is it short. Then she kneels, then gets up and recites. When she finishes reciting, she says “Allahu Akbar” four times, then she kneels. On the fourth"
"5755","(5755) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Ma’bad bin Khalid, on the authority of Kurdous, who said: Sa’id bin Al-Aas presented In Dhul-Hijjah, he sent to Abdullah, Hudhayf, Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, and Abu Musa Al-Ash’ari. So he asked them about the takbir during Eid? So they entrusted their affairs to Abdullah, and Abdullah said: He gets up and says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”. So he recites, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, and he kneels, and he gets up and recites, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, then he says “Allahu Akbar”. He says “Allahu Akbar” the fourth time, then he bows."
"5756","(5756) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, they said: Nine takbeers, and he continues between the two Qir’ānahs."
"5757","(5757) Hushaym told us, he said: Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: Ibn Abbas led the prayer for us on the day of Eid. Then he said “Allahu Akbar” nine times. Five in the first, four in the last, and a wali between the two qira’at."
"5758","(5758) Hushaym told us, he said: Dawud told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Ziyad sent to Masruq: We are busy with business. So, how to say “Allahu Akbar” on the two Eids? He said: Nine takbeers. He said: Five in the first, four in the last, and a vowel between the two Qur’anic verses."
"5759","(5759) Ghandar and Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, and Masruq; They used to say “Allahu Akbar” nine times during the Eid."
"5760","(5760) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” nine times during the Eid. He mentioned the example of the hadith of Abdullah."
"5761","(5761) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; The companions of Abdullah used to say “Allahu Akbar” nine times during the two Eids."
"5762","(5762) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, who said: The takbir in the two Eids is nine times."
"5763","(5763) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far; He used to issue fatwas according to the words of Abdullah regarding the takbeer of the two Eids."
"5764","(5764) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He said: The takbeer in the Eid al-Adha and the Eid is seven and five in the two Eids, both before the recitation, no. Between the two Qaraites."
"5765","(5765) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They used to say “Allahu Akbar” nine times."
"5766","(5766) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar; In the two Eids, in one of them there are nine takbirs, and in the other there are eleven."
"5767","(5767) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Rafi’. Omar ibn al-Khattab used to say “Allahu Akbar” on the twelve days of the Eids. Seven in the first, and five in the last."
"5768","(5768) Omar bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar, on the authority of his father; He used to say “Allahu Akbar” seven and five times during the Eid. Seven in the first, and five in the last."
"5769","(5769) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habib told us, he said: Dawud informed us Ibn al-Husayn, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sa`id al-Khudri, who said: The takbir in the two Eids is seven and five; Seven in the first before the recitation, and five in the last before the recitation."
"5770","(5770) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Nafi’ bin Abi Nu’aym told us, he said: I heard Nafi’, he said: Abdullah bin Omar said: The takbeer in the two Eids is seven and five."
"5771","(5771) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Hilal narrated to us, saying: I heard Salim bin Abdullah and Abdullah bin Abd. God commanded Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Dahhak on the Day of Fitr, and Medina was required to say “Allahu Akbar” seven times in the first rak’ah. Then he recites: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High} and in the last five, then he recites: {Read in the name of your Lord who created}"
"5772","(5772) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Thabit bin Qais told us, he said: I prayed behind Omar bin Abdul Aziz Al-Fitr, so he said the takbir. In the first there are seven before the recitation, and in the second there are five before the recitation."
"5773","(5773) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Humaid informed us, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Ammar; That Ibn Abbas said the takbeer on Eid twelve days; Seven in the first, and five in the last."
"5774","(5774) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Abu Kudayna narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Al-Musayyab, they said: : The prayer on the day of the two Eids consists of nine takbeers; Five in the first, and four in the last, there is no major difference between the two recitations."
"5775","(5775) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, he said: Damra bin Saeed told us, he said: I heard Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, saying: Omar went out on the day of Eid, and he asked Abu Waqid Al-Laythi: What did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recite? And he greeted him on this day? He said: With: (Q), and (I approached). (Tirmidhi 5351, Ibn Majah 1282)"
"5776","(5776) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite during the two Eid and Friday prayers: {Has the hadith of the cheater reached you?} And {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High} And when the two sticks come together on a day, it is recited between them."
"5777","(5777) Waki` ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ma`abad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Zayd ibn Uqba, on the authority of Samurah ibn grasshopper; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the two Eids: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High} and {Have He come to you? Hadith of Al-Ghashiya}"
"5778","(5778) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ma’abad ibn Khalid, on the authority of Zayd ibn Uqba, on the authority of Samurah ibn grasshopper; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite during the two Eids, so he mentioned something similar to it. (Tabarani 6778)"
"5779","(5779) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father (h) and on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawus; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited during the Eid. One of them said: B: (it approached), and the other said: B: (Q)"
"5780","(5780) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas; On the day of Eid al-Baqarah, Abu Bakr recited Al-Baqarah until I saw the sheikh standing up for a long time."
"5781","(5781) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: I narrated on the authority of Omar; He used to recite during the Eid: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and {Has the hadith of Al-Gashiya reached you}."
"5782","(5782) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite during the Eid: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Has there come to you a hadith? Al-Ghashiya}"
"5783","(5783) Hushaym and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Kurdous, on the authority of Abdullah; Al-Walid bin Uqba sent to him and said: You should recite Umm Al-Kitab and a surah from Al-Mufassal. Hashim added to it: not from its shortness, nor from its length."
"5784","(5784) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Ammar al-Saydalani told us, on the authority of a servant of Anas who named him, he said: I stayed with Anas on the day of the Eid, until we came to the corner. When he turned away from him, it is recited on the Eid as: {Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High}, and {Has the hadith of the cheater reached you}, and Anas said: They are the two surahs with which the Messenger of God recited. May God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 2046)"
"5785","(5785) Waki` and Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on the day of Eid and led the people in prayer, but he did not pray before them, nor After her (Bukhari 989. Abu Dawud 1152)"
"5786","(5786) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah Al-Bajli, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He went out on the day of Eid and did not pray before or after it, and he mentioned that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did so. (Tirmidhi 538)"
"5787","(5787) Ibn Idris and Ibn Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Awfa, and Ibn Umar, Jabir bin Abdullah, Shurayh, and Ibn Maqil do not pray before or after Eid."
"5788","(5788) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I was with him sitting in the Sacred Mosque. On the day of Fitr, Ataa stood up and prayed before the imam came out, so Saeed sent to him: Sit, so Ataa sat. He said: So I said to Saeed: Who is this about, O Abu Abdullah? He said: On the authority of Hudhayf and his companions."
"5789","(5789) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Sami’, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Kathir; That Abu Masoud Al-Ansari used to go around the rows and say: There is no prayer except with Imam"
"5790","(5790) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, on the authority of Tha’labah ibn Zahid Al-Hanzali; Abu Masoud Al-Ansari got up on the day of Eid and said: There is no prayer on this day until the imam comes out."
"5791","(5791) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not pray before or after Eid."
"5792","(5792) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: I was between a robbed and a mutilated man. On the day of Eid, they did not pray before it or after it."
"5793","(5793) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He did not pray before the Eid, nor After him"
"5794","(5794) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: Al-Sha’bi saw a person praying after the imam had left. So he took it away."
"5795","(5795) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Salamah, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: There is no prayer before it or after it."
"5796","(5796) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He did not pray before or after it."
"5797","(5797) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Umar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: There is no prayer before it, nor After her"
"5798","(5798) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Abdullah al-Asam; He went out with Masruq on the day of Eid, and I stood up to pray, and he took my clothes and made me sit, then he said: There is no prayer until The imam prays."
"5799","(5799) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr, Ibrahim, and Alqamah were praying. Four days after the Eid."
"5800","(5800) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Ibrahim and Sa’id bin Jubair, Mujahid, and Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla pray four times after it."
"5801","(5801) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Alqama used to come on the day of Eid and sit. In the place of prayer, and he does not pray until the imam prays, so when the imam prays, he stands and prays four times."
"5802","(5802) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayy, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: I heard him say: When Abdullah He returned on the day of Eid and prayed four times for his family."
"5803","(5803) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Hilal, who said: I went out with Ali, and when he prayed The imam stood up and prayed four more prayers."
"5804","(5804) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, and the companions of Abdullah; They used to pray four times after the Eid."
"5805","(5805) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to pray four times after the Eid, and no They pray something before it."
"5806","(5806) Abdi told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin praying after the Eid, and spending a long time. Resurrection"
"5807","(5807) Shababah bin Suwar narrated to us, saying: Al-Mughirah bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida, on the authority of his father ; On the day of Eid, he used to pray four times before the prayer and four after it."
"5808","(5808) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Al-Aswad used to pray before The two Eids. He said: Alqamah did not pray before it, but he prayed four times after it."
"5809","(5809) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Enough with the words of Abdullah, It means in prayer after Eid."
"5810","(5810) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Anas Ibn Malik and Al-Hasan praying before they set out. Imam It means the day of Eid."
"5811","(5811) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders; That Abu Barza used to pray on Eid before the imam."
"5812","(5812) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi. He saw Anas, Al-Hasan, Saeed bin Abi Al-Hasan, and Jabir bin Zaid praying before the imam on the two Eids."
"5813","(5813) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Danaj, who said: I saw Abu Barza doing it."
"5814","(5814) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He used to pray on the Day of Breakfast and the Day of Sacrifice before the Imam appeared."
"5815","(5815) Gandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of al-Hikam, on the authority of lions; He used to pray on the day of Eid before the imam came out."
"5816","(5816) Saul bin Yusuf narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Azraq bin Qais, on the authority of a man, who said: I saw men among the companions of They came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Eid, and they prayed before the imam."
"5817","(5817) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Khalid Al-Ahdab, on the authority of his uncle Safwan bin Mahrez, who said: It was a prayer Safwan on the day of Fitr and Sacrifice is ten rak'ahs before the imam emerges, two rak'ahs with the imam, and two rak'ahs after the imam."
"5818","(5818) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, he said: I saw Anas, Al-Hasan, and Saeed bin Abi Al-Hasan. They pray on the day of Eid before the imam."
"5819","(5819) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whenever he recited during the two Eids He listens to those who follow him, but he does not speak out loud."
"5820","(5820) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The voice is raised when reciting recitation in Friday prayers and Eid prayers."
"5821","(5821) Jarir and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: Washing on the day of sacrifice And the day of breaking the fast."
"5822","(5822) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Zazan; That a man asked Ali about washing? He said: Washing on the day of Eid al-Adha and on the day of Eid al-Fitr."
"5823","(5823) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, he said: Abdullah bin Omar told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to wash himself for the Eids."
"5824","(5824) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Sinan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He took a bath on the two Eids."
"5825","(5825) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to wash himself on the two Eids."
"5826","(5826) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to wash himself on the Day of Breakfast and on the Day of Sacrifice."
"5827","(5827) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They used to wash themselves on the Day of Breakfast and the Day of Sacrifice."
"5828","(5828) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, He said: They liked to wash themselves on the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Breakfast."
"5829","(5829) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, that he heard him say: Bathing. The Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Fitr before you leave is due."
"5830","(5830) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Bakr; That Salem bin Abdullah used to wash himself for Eid."
"5831","(5831) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Bakr, he said: I heard Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah order By washing for the two Eids."
"5832","(5832) Waki’ and Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of his father; He used to recommend washing for Friday prayers and the Eid prayers."
"5833","(5833) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He used to wash himself on the day of Eid before he went to bed."
"5834","(5834) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abbas, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he brings his daughters and wives out for the Eid. (Ibn Majah 1309. Ahmad 1/354)"
"5835","(5835) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Talha Al-Yami, he said: Abu Bakr said: A right over every person. The scope of going out to the two Eids."
"5836","(5836) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is the right of every living being to go out. To the two Eids, and he did not give them any permission to go out except for the two Eids."
"5837","(5837) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Abdullah ibn Umar used to go out to the Eids from He was able to help his family."
"5838","(5838) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, who said: Aisha said: Al-Ka’ab used to go out to the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace from her chambers during breaking the fast and the sacrifice. (Ahmad 6/184, Ibn Rahawi 1358)"
"5839","(5839) Yahya bin Sulaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Mujahid, regarding his saying: (Kawa’ib) he said: Nawahid."
"5840","(5840) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Aswad; Alqamiya and Al-Aswad used to take their wives out during the two Eids and prevent them from having sexual intercourse with them."
"5841","(5841) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: If Abu Ishaq’s wife was willing, she would go out to the Eid."
"5842","(5842) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Alqamiya had a woman who had passed the age who would go out to The two Eids."
"5843","(5843) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiya, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that we should bring them out on the Day of Breakfast and on the Day of Sacrifice. Umm Atiyya said: So we said: Have you seen one of them? Does she have a robe? He said: Let her sister wear her jilbab. (Bukhari 324, Abu Dawud 1131)"
"5844","(5844) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for women to go out during the Eids."
"5845","(5845) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Jabir, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not take his wives out during the two Eids."
"5846","(5846) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He would not let a woman from his family go out to break the fast or to sacrifice the sacrifice."
"5847","(5847) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim narrated to us, he said: Al-Qasim was the most severe on me. He does not allow freed slaves to go out during breaking the fast and the sacrifice."
"5848","(5848) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is disliked for a young woman to go out to The two Eids."
"5849","(5849) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: He prays four times."
"5850","(5850) Hushaym and Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, who said: Abdullah said: Whoever missed the Eid Let him pray four times."
"5851","(5851) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He prays four times."
"5852","(5852) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He prays two rak’ahs and says “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5853","(5853) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, he said: Some of the family of Anas told me; Perhaps Anas gathered his family and members of his family on the day of Eid, and Abdullah bin Abi Utba led two rak’ahs of prayer with them."
"5854","(5854) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Abu Iyad was hiding, he said: Mujahid came to him. On the day of Eid, he prayed two rak’ahs and supplicated."
"5855","(5855) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Whoever has an excuse will be excused on the Day of Judgment. Iftar, Friday prayer, or Eid al-Adha, its prayer is four rak’ahs."
"5856","(5856) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Abu Omar, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, he said: He prays two rak’ahs."
"5857","(5857) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He prays like the prayer of the imam."
"5858","(5858) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you miss praying with the imam, pray something like His prayers"
"5859","(5859) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad; Whoever does not know how to pray on the day of Eid, he said: He should pray like his prayer, and he should say “Allahu Akbar” like his “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5860","(5860) A partner told us, he said: I asked Abu Ishaq about a man who comes on the day of Eid and the imam has finished? He said: He prays two rak'ahs."
"5861","(5861) Hassan bin Abdul Rahman Al Harithi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning the one who misses the Eid, he said: It was desirable for him to pray like the imam’s prayer, and if he knew what the imam recited, he would recite it. With it"
"5862","(5862) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: If you miss the Eid prayer, perform a rak’ah. So perform it, and do with it what the imam does in the first rak’ah."
"5863","(5863) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He says “Allahu Akbar” with him in this matter as he catches you from it. He makes up for what he missed and says “Allahu Akbar” in it, just like the Imam says “Allahu Akbar” in the second rak’ah."
"5864","(5864) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Hanash, who said: It was said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: Indeed, it is double. Because of the weakness of the people, they are not able to go out to the graveyard, so he ordered a man to lead the people in prayer four rak’ahs; Two rak'ahs for Eid, and two rak'ahs for the place of their departure to the graveyard."
"5865","(5865) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; That Ali ordered a man to lead two rak’ahs of people in prayer in the mosque."
"5866","(5866) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, who said: I think it is, on the authority of Huzayl; That Ali ordered a man to lead four people in prayer on the day of Eid, like the Hajr prayer."
"5867","(5867) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Layla said: He led the people in prayer in the Kufa Mosque in two rak’ahs, during the rule of Musab bin Al-Zubair."
"5868","(5868) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila; That Ali ordered a man to lead the people in prayer in the Kufa Mosque in two rak’ahs. He said: Ibn Abi Layla said: He prays two rak’ahs, and a man said to Ibn Abi Layla: He prays without a sermon? He said: Yes."
"5869","(5869) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: Muslim bin Yazid bin Dhūkūr al-Kāriqī narrated to us, saying: Al-Qasim bin Abd led us in prayer. On the day of Eid, the Most Gracious, he performed two rak’ahs in the Grand Mosque and delivered a sermon."
"5870","(5870) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Arif bin Dirham, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Abi Dhail coming. The Great Mosque on the day of Eid."
"5871","(5871) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: He says “Allahu Akbar”, then he gets up and makes up, then he says “Allahu Akbar”."
"5872","(5872) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He makes up the prayer, then says “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5873","(5873) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, saying: I saw Ibn Shubarmah more than once, when he missed any part of the prayer for several days. Al-Tashreeq stood up and said it, then he said “Allahu Akbar”."
"5874","(5874) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to say: “Allahu Akbar” with him, then he would stand up. Then it will be decided."
"5875","(5875) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; Concerning a man who misses the rak’ah on the days of Tashreeq, Ibn Sirin said: He makes up for it, then he says “Allahu Akbar”, and Al-Hasan said: He pronounces “Allahu Akbar”. Then it will be decided."
"5876","(5876) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If you miss a rak’ah On the days of Tashreeq, do not say “Allahu Akbar” until you complete them."
"5877","(5877) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He says “Allahu Akbar” with the imam, then he fulfills what came before. With it"
"5878","(5878) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to say: He fulfills what he missed, then he says “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5879","(5879) Hakam al-Razi told us, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He says “Allahu Akbar” with the imam, then he says “Allahu Akbar” when he finishes. Abu Bakr said: And I was informed that this is what Ibn Abi Layla said."
"5880","(5880) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he prays alone, or in a group, or voluntarily, He grew up"
"5881","(5881) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He does not say takbir unless he prays in it. All together"
"5882","(5882) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammam, who said: I saw his followers praying alone during the days of Tashreeq, so he said “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5883","(5883) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: “Say takbeer in voluntary prayers even if you pray alone.”"
"5884","(5884) Hakam al-Razi told us, on the authority of Anbasa, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The takbeer on the days of sunrise in every voluntary and obligatory."
"5885","(5885) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: They were They say “Allahu Akbar” after the two rak’ahs on the Day of Sacrifice."
"5886","(5886) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Ja’far, on the authority of Wahb bin Kaysan, who said: ‘Aidan gathered During the reign of Ibn al-Zubayr, he delayed going out, then he went out and delivered a sermon, and he prolonged the sermon, then he prayed, and did not go out until Friday, so some people criticized him, so that reached Ibn Abbas, and he said: He is correct in the Sunnah. Then Ibn al-Zubayr reached the news and said: I witnessed the Eid with Omar, and he did as I did. (Abu Dawud 1064, An-Nasa’i 1794)"
"5887","(5887) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Ubaid, a client of Ibn Azhar, who said: I witnessed The Eid with Uthman, and the day of Friday came together, so he said: This is a day on which two Eids for the Muslims were gathered, so who was he? We are from the people of Al-Awali. We have given him permission to depart, and whoever wishes to stay, let him stay."
"5888","(5888) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Ala, on the authority of Abi Abd Al-Rahman, who said: Two leaders gathered to make a covenant with Ali. So he led the people in prayer, then he delivered a sermon on his mount, then he said: O people, whoever of you attends the Eid has performed the Friday prayer. God willing"
"5889","(5889) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father, who said: Two of Ali’s covenants gathered together and he bore witness to them. Eid, then he said: Indeed, they are gathered, so whoever wants to witness, let him witness."
"5890","(5890) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Habib bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite in the two Eids: {Glorify the name of your Lord Most High}, and {Has a hadith come to you? Al-Ghashiya}, and when the two sticks come together on a day, it is recited between them."
"5891","(5891) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Wahb ibn Kaysan, who said: Two sticks gathered one day. So Abdullah bin Al-Zubair went out and prayed the Eid prayer after the day had risen, then he entered and did not leave until he had prayed the afternoon prayer. Hisham said: I mentioned that to Nafi’, or it was mentioned to him, and he said: This was mentioned to Ibn Umar, but he did not deny it."
"5892","(5892) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Two ‘Aidans gathered during the reign of Ibn al-Zubayr and he led them in prayer. Eid, then he led the Dhuhr prayer with them in congregation, four times."
"5893","(5893) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: Two leaders gathered at the time of al-Hajjaj, and one of them prayed, and he said Abu Al-Bakhtari: May God kill him because he commented on this?"
"5894","(5894) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The former of the two is sufficient."
"5895","(5895) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If two sticks come together on a day, then whichever one you bring I reward you"
"5896","(5896) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Uthman al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ramla al-Shamimi, who said: I witnessed with Muawiyah. Zaid bin Arqam is asked: Did you witness with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on two occasions when they met? He said: Yes, he said: How did he do it? He said: He prayed the Eid prayer, then he made a concession in congregation. He said: Whoever wants to pray, let him pray. (Abu Dawud 1063. Ahmad 4/372)"
"5897","(5897) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, who said: The two camels gathered together one day, and the pilgrims stood up. The first Eid, so he said: Whoever wants to gather with us, let him gather, and whoever wants to leave, let him leave, and there is no blame. Abu Al-Bakhtari and Maysara: What is the matter with him? May God Almighty fight him. Where did this happen to him?"
"5898","(5898) Zayd ibn Harun told us, he said: Al-Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ali (h) and on the authority of Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Abraham; On the two Eids when they come together? They said: One of them is sufficient."
"5899","(5899) Yazeed bin Harun told us, he said: Hajjaj told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Al-Zubayr, he said: One or the other is sufficient."
"5900","(5900) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, he said: If it is a Friday A promise, one more than the other."
"5901","(5901) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Omar, who said: The prayer of a journey is two rak’ahs, and the prayer is combined. Two rak'ahs, and the two rituals are two rak'ahs, complete without shortening, according to the words of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ibn Majah 1063. An-Nasa’i 1733)"
"5902","(5902) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out on the day of Eid al-Fitr, or the sacrifice of sacrifice, and led the people in two rak’ahs of prayer, then he left, and did not He should pray before it or after it."
"5903","(5903) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, he said: Iyad bin Abdullah bin Abi Sarh narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Saeed, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go out on the day of Eid, the day of breaking the fast, and lead the people in prayer. Two rak'ahs, then he says the salutation. (Muslim 6050, An-Nasa’i 1785)"
"5904","(5904) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Qais, on the authority of Iyad, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, he delivered a speech on his camel on the day of Eid. (Abu Ali 1177. Ibn Hibban 2825)"
"5905","(5905) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Misra Abi Jamilah, who said: I witnessed the Eid with Ali, and when He prayed and addressed his mount. He said: And Othman used to do it."
"5906","(5906) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, who said: Ali led the Eid with us, then He addressed his mount."
"5907","(5907) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Qays, who said: I saw Al-Mughirah bin His people are addressing Bakhtiya."
"5908","(5908) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abu Kahil, he said: I saw the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, delivering a speech to an old she-camel, and an Ethiopian holding her reins. (Ibn Majah 1284. Ahmad 4/306)"
"5909","(5909) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab. On the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ghanam, on the authority of Amr bin Kharijah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, addressed them while he was on his camel. He said: And his camel is clogged with its water, and its saliva is dripping between my shoulders. (Tirmidhi 2121. Ahmad 4/187)"
"5910","(5910) Hashim bin Al-Qasim narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, he said: Al-Harmas bin Ziyad narrated to us, he said: I was my father’s buttocks. The Day of Sacrifice, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, addresses a camel with manna. (Bukhari 2883. Abu Dawud 1949)"
"5911","(5911) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Shu`bi, he said: Ali addressed us on the same day. Eid on his camel."
"5912","(5912) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Imam used to begin the day of Eid. He prays, then rides and delivers the sermon."
"5913","(5913) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, that he heard him mention it. He said: I saw al-Mughirah ibn Sha'bah delivers sermons to the people on the day of Eid, on the back of a camel."
"5914","(5914) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He liked for women to say “Allahu Akbar” after prayer. The days of the East."
"5915","(5915) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan did not consider pronouncing takbeer on women in the days of al-Tashreeq."
"5916","(5916) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman Al Qari, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah bin Utba, he said: It is Sunnah for the imam to say “Allahu Akbar” on the pulpit on the two Eids nine days before the sermon, and seven After that (Abdul Razzaq 5672)"
"5917","(5917) Abu Dawud Al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Abi Al-Hasana, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He says “Allahu Akbar” on the Day of Resurrection. The two Eids are fourteen days of greatness."
"5918","(5918) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair ibn Amir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He performs tayammum for the two men. And the funeral."
"5919","(5919) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Najih, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Qasim; Concerning a man who misses the Eid and is afraid of missing it. He said: He performs tayammum and prays if he is afraid."
"5920","(5920) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man speaking on the day of Eid, he said: He asks for water and performs ablution, but does not perform tayammum."
"5921","(5921) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ata’ al-Khurasani told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, he said: It was the prayer that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to burn the night prayer for those who missed it, the evening prayer."
"5922","(5922) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Hamid, and others, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The prayer was Which the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to burn the Friday prayer for those who neglected it."
"5923","(5923) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, in a hadith he mentioned on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: These are the evening and dawn prayers. (Bukhari 644. An-Nasa’i 921)"
"5924","(5924) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, he said: He heard it from him, On the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said: This is the congregation."
"5925","(5925) Saal bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, he said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about the people who are in Al-Rustaq and the Eid is attending them. Will they gather and have a man lead them in prayer? And about the gathering? So he wrote to me: As for the Eid, they gather together and a man leads them in prayer, but as for the gathering, I have no knowledge of it."
"5926","(5926) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah; He said about people being in black while traveling on the day of Eid al-Fitr or Eid al-Adha. He said: They gather. They pray, and one of them leads them in prayer."
"5927","(5927) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the people of the villages and the people of Sawad attending the Eid, he said: He did not think they should go out and have a man lead them in prayer."
"5928","(5928) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Ata bin Abi was asked Rabah? He said: If it is a congregational village, then they should pray two rak’ahs like on a Friday prayer.\n Yahya said: Al-Hakam bin Utaiba was asked? He said: There is no congregational prayer except with the imam in the mosque.\n Yahya said, and his leaders said: I do not know of the congregation except with the Sultan in the Muslim lands.\n Yahya said: It is said: No Friday prayer, no sacrifice, no breaking the fast except for those who are present with the imam."
"5929","(5929) Muammar bin Sulaiman Al-Ruqi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to the family of The villagers commanded them to perform the Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha prayers, and to gather them together."
"5930","(5930) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If the town has an emir May the Friday prayer be upon them."
"5931","(5931) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Aqmar, who said: Masruq came out, and Urwah bin Al-Mughirah went to a Bedouin of theirs. He said: Then the gathering came, but they did not gather, and the breaking of the fast came, but they did not break the fast."
"5932","(5932) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of someone who heard Ata’ and Mujahid, who said: The takbir is decreed in The two Eids, just as the prayer is performed."
"5933","(5933) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He prays two rak’ahs and says “Allahu Akbar.”"
"5934","(5934) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He prays like his prayer, and says “Allahu Akbar” like Takbeerah"
"5935","(5935) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, he said: They used to say: If he doubts The man was praying the Maghrib prayer and wanted to perform the Eid prayer. He prayed one rak’ah and made it interceded, then he prayed three more."
"5936","(5936) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Qasim, the same."
"5937","(5937) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, who said: He took Ziyad bin Abi by the hand. Al-Ja'd, and he brought me to a sheikh with a ruqyah, called: Wabasa bin Ma'bad, and he said: A man prayed behind the row alone, so he ordered him to do so. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to celebrate Eid. (Tirmidh 230. Ahmad 4/228)"
"5938","(5938) Mulazim bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, he said: Abdul Rahman bin Ali bin Shayban narrated to me, on the authority of His father, Ali bin Shayban, who was part of the delegation, said: We went out until we came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So we pledged allegiance to him and prayed behind him, and he saw a man praying behind the row alone, so the Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stood over him. He gave the salutation until he left, then he said: Continue your prayer, for there is no prayer for the one behind the row."
"5939","(5939) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Marwan, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He celebrates Eid."
"5940","(5940) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He does not stand alone."
"5941","(5941) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Shu’abi narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Murra: on the authority of Hilal bin Yasaf, on the authority of Amr bin Rashid, On the authority of Wabisa bin Ma’abad; A man prayed behind the rows alone, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to repeat the prayer. (Abu Dawud 682. Ahmad 4/228)"
"5942","(5942) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Ad-Dahhak, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: He was asked about a man who prayed behind the rows. Alone? He said: He will not celebrate Eid."
"5943","(5943) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, and Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It is sufficient."
"5944","(5944) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man entering the mosque but not being able to enter the row. He said: He thought that would be sufficient if he prayed. behind him"
"5945","(5945) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhiyal, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who performs a rak’ah first and speaks to the imam, so he takes the hand of the one who preceded him and leads him in. How is he to do that? He said: He prays one rak'ah and sits, then he builds on the people's prayer. When he completes four rak'ahs with them, he sits and recites, then takes In the hand of a man, so he said the salutations, then the man stood up and prayed the rak’ah that he had performed previously."
"5946","(5946) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Shaqri, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who prayed one rak’ah and started it, so he took a man’s hand and brought him forward, and he had missed that rak’ah, and he said: He will lead them in prayer. For the remainder of their prayer, when he had finished, he took the hand of a man who had witnessed that rak’ah, brought him forward and greeted them, then stood up and performed it. That rak'ah"
"5947","(5947) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Arqam bin Shurahbil, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to Abu Bakr while he was praying during his illness, he took from the Qur’an from Where he reached Abu Bakr. (Ahmad 1/355)"
"5948","(5948) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; Concerning a man who started the prayer, so he took another man’s hand and brought him forward, saying: His recitation is sufficient if he recited, and his takbeer is sufficient if he recited, and his takbeer is sufficient if he recited. He was arrogant"
"5949","(5949) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Al-Hasan used to say regarding what the imam presented: If he wants, he can read from where the imam left off, and if he wants, he can select some surahs."
"5950","(5950) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith bin Abi Dirar, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab ; Concerning a man who, when he was praying, said: He should turn his back and perform ablution, then come back and pray, and he should continue his past."
"5951","(5951) Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: A sheikh from the people of hadith narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Bakr, with a similar saying. Omar"
"5952","(5952) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man trembles during his prayer, Or he vomits, let him perform ablution and not speak, but continue his prayer."
"5953","(5953) Hushaym told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever has a temper in Let him leave his prayer and perform ablution. If he does not speak, he continues his prayer, and if he speaks, he resumes the prayer."
"5954","(5954) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Imran bin Dhabyan, on the authority of Abu Tahya Hakim bin Saad, on the authority of Salman, he said: If one of you interrupts the prayer, let him leave, unaware of his action, and perform ablution, then return to the prayer. The verses that he used to recite."
"5955","(5955) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ali bin Salih and Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, On the authority of Ali, he said: If one of you feels rice, vomiting, or nosebleeds in his stomach, let him leave, perform ablution, then Let him continue his prayers as long as he does not speak."
"5956","(5956) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Alqama felt weak during prayer, so he took a man’s hand and led him forward, then he went and performed ablution, then he came back and built on what was left. His prayers"
"5957","(5957) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, who said: If a man shudders during his prayer, he goes away and performs ablution. Then he built on what remained of his prayer."
"5958","(5958) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, who said: I saw Salem ibn Abdullah performing the lunch prayer in one rak’ah. Then he shook his head, went out and performed ablution, then came back and continued the remainder of his prayer."
"5959","(5959) Hushaym and Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, and Al-Shu’abi, that they said In the case of a severe case or nosebleed: he leaves and performs ablution. If he speaks, he resumes the prayer, and if he does not speak, he continues his prayer."
"5960","(5960) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; He used to say about someone who shuddered in his prayer, he said: He should leave and perform ablution, then build on what remained of his prayer. He did not speak, so if he spoke, he resumed the prayer."
"5961","(5961) Hushaym told us, saying: Abdul-Malik told us about Ata’; He said something like that."
"5962","(5962) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; In the case of one who is vomiting, having nosebleeds, and kissing: he leaves and performs ablution. If he does not speak, he continues on as long as he remains, and if he speaks He resumed. And he used to say about the one who defecates and urinates: Should he leave and perform ablution, and begin the prayer??"
"5963","(5963) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: They used to be strict about defecation and urination. They believe that it is worse than semen and blood."
"5964","(5964) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, that he used to say: If a man shudders during his prayer, then He leaves and performs ablution, then comes and continues on as he did before, as long as he does not speak if he wants. If he does, he repeats the ablution. And he repeated the prayer."
"5965","(5965) Hushaym told us, saying: Abd al-Hamid al-Madani informed us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, he said: I saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab shaking his head while he was praying, so he came to the house of Umm Salama, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He performed ablution without speaking, and continued his prayer."
"5966","(5966) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Amir, who said: If you break the prayer, pray What remains, even if you speak."
"5967","(5967) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a man who was afflicted with vomiting and nosebleeds while praying, he said: He should turn his head and perform ablution, then continue his prayer unless He speaks."
"5968","(5968) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Mu’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, with something like this, except He did not mention vomiting."
"5969","(5969) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They are unanimously agreed that when he speaks, he resumes And I would love for him to speak and resume the prayer."
"5970","(5970) Abu Bakr narrated to us, he said: Rabi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If a man turns towards the qiblah, he faces, and if he turns away On his right, or on his left, he continued his prayer."
"5971","(5971) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: What is most beloved to me is the nose-bleed when it turns away. The one who accepts it is to receive it."
"5972","(5972) Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his uncle, who said: I have come quickly. Abdullah bin Masoud was in it, but I found him praying. Between Maghrib and Isha, and he used to say: This is an hour of negligence."
"5973","(5973) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of his brother Abdullah bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amr, he said: The prayer of the followers of the night prayer takes place between the time when the people of the Maghrib shrouds and the time when they return to dinner."
"5974","(5974) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Badr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’athai, who said: Salman said: You should pray between the two evening prayers, for it will relieve one of you of his burden and keep him away from it. Its cancellation is at the beginning of the night, for its cancellation at the beginning of the night is a period of calm, or a departure for its end."
"5975","(5975) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Waqi’ ibn Iyas, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr; He used to pray between Maghrib and Isha', and he would say: This is the beginning of the night."
"5976","(5976) Abdullah bin Daoud narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih; He used to pray between Maghrib and Isha."
"5977","(5977) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Amara bin Zazan, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas; He used to pray between Maghrib and Isha', and he would say: This is the beginning of the night."
"5978","(5978) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: Al-Hasan bin Muslim used to pray often. Between Maghrib and Isha, he said: Al-Hasan claimed that Tawus did not see anything."
"5979","(5979) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Why It can be counted as part of the night prayer."
"5980","(5980) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; Abdullah bin Omar would not lead her in prayer except during Ramadan, meaning between Maghrib and Isha."
"5981","(5981) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; In his saying: {Their sides should avoid their beds} He said: They used to volunteer between the two prayers; Maghrib and Isha', so they pray."
"5982","(5982) Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Misra ibn Habib al-Nahdi, on the authority of al-Manhal, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I prayed Maghrib with him, then he stood up and prayed until Isha prayer (Tirmidhi 3781, Ahmad 5/404)"
"5983","(5983) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Thawair bin Abi Fakhita, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, he said: It was mentioned to him that between Maghrib and Isha' there was a prayer of heedlessness, so Ali said: You fell in heedlessness."
"5984","(5984) Waki’ told us, he said: Musa bin Ubaidah told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever prays For four days after sunset, it was like one following one battle after another."
"5985","(5985) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, who said: I prayed next to Al-Hasan. Ibn Ali prayed the Maghrib prayer, then I prayed two rak’ahs after the sunset prayer, then I stood up to pray and he rebuked me and said: It was only two rak’ahs."
"5986","(5986) Abu Bakr told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told us, he said: I heard an alcoholic person saying: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever prays two rak’ahs after sunset, meaning before he speaks, his prayer will be offered in Aliyah."
"5987","(5987) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Asim al-Asadi, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, who said: I have neglected, or if I had neglected, the two rak’ahs after sunset, I would have feared that I would not be forgiven."
"5988","(5988) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Fudail bin Ghazwan narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to live between noon and afternoon."
"5989","(5989) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They were They liken the evening prayer, and what is between noon and afternoon prayer, to the night prayer."
"5990","(5990) Abdullah bin Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Bukair bin Amir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Abdullah used to pray between Dhuhr and Asr."
"5991","(5991) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Salih, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Four Rakats before noon are equivalent to the dawn prayer."
"5992","(5992) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, he said: Abu Ayyub Al-Ansari said: O Messenger of God, what are the four rak’ahs that you perform regularly before noon? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The gates of Paradise are opened at noon, so do not shake until the prayer is performed. I would like to present. (Abu Dawud 1264, Ahmad 5/416)"
"5993","(5993) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Salt, On the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly. (Bukhari 2403. Ahmad 5/418)"
"5994","(5994) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qais, on the authority of Aoun ibn Abdullah ibn Utba, on the authority of his father, he said: I prayed With Omar, he performed four rak'ahs before noon in his house."
"5995","(5995) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, were not May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, they should leave four rak’ahs before noon, and two rak’ahs before dawn in every situation."
"5996","(5996) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Four before noon. He makes peace between them unless he becomes a witness."
"5997","(5997) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Sakhrah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Utba, who said: I saw Omar praying four times. Before noon."
"5998","(5998) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza, on the authority of Ibn Abi Nimr, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He used to pray four times before that."
"5999","(5999) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Bashir, on the authority of a sheikh from the Ansar, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever prays four times before noon will have the same freedom as a slave from the descendants of Ismail. (Tabarani 965)"
"6000","(6000) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Ammar, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to pray four times before noon."
"6001","(6001) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Al-Asbagh, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He used to pray four times before her."
"6002","(6002) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed four times before noon. (Bukhari 1182 and Abu Dawud 1247)"
"6003","(6003) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, he said: My father sent to Aisha: What is the prayer? Was it most beloved to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he be constant with her? She said: He used to pray four times before noon, during which he would stand for a long time, and do good bowing and prostration during them."
"6004","(6004) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar praying four times before noon, It prolongs it."
"6005","(6005) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, similarly."
"6006","(6006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi; Al-Hasan bin Ali used to pray four times before noon, and he spent a long time praying them. Abu Aoun said: If he is slow in reading, then he is tall, and if he is slow in reading, then he is meen."
"6007","(6007) Ibn Abi Ghaniyah told us, on the authority of Al-Salt ibn Bahram, on the authority of the one who told him, on the authority of Hudhayf ibn Asid, he said: I saw Ali, when the sun has passed, pray four long times."
"6008","(6008) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Budil, he said: Abtan narrated to me. People refer to Abdullah bin Masoud: He used to pray four rak’ahs in his house when the sun went down, and he would perform them for a long time. When the muezzins respond, he goes out and sits in the mosque until the prayer is performed."
"6009","(6009) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’, on the authority of a man; Omar recited in the four hours before noon: (Q)."
"6010","(6010) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab bin Rafi’; That Abu Ayyub used to pray eight rak’ahs before noon."
"6011","(6011) Abdă told us, on the authority of Ubad Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to pray eight rak'ahs before noon."
"6012","(6012) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to pray four days after noon."
